Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"ज़मीन के ऊपर हिमाल रहती थी, एक राजकुमारी — दयालु, होशियार, और इतनी अकेली जितना किसी को अंदाज़ा भी न था। कहानियाँ चाहे जैसे भी शुरू हों, वे सब एक दिन उसे उसी चश्मे के किनारे ले आती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Above the ground lived Himal, a princess — kind, clever, and lonelier than anyone knew. The tellings begin in different ways, but they all bring her, one day, to the edge of that spring.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"और वहाँ उसने उसे देखा — और उसने उसे देखा — और दोनों दुनियाओं के बीच का पानी जैसे गायब ही हो गया। वे तब तक बातें करते रहे जब तक परछाइयाँ ढलने नहीं लगीं। वह अपने राज्य से ऊपर आया; वह अपने महल से नीचे आई; और पुरानी कहानियों के दस्तूर के मुताबिक, यानी पलक झपकते ही, दोनों को एक-दूसरे से प्यार हो गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And there she saw him — and he saw her — and the water between the two worlds might as well not have been there. They talked till the shadows moved. He came up from his kingdom; she came down from her palace; and by the old measure of such things, which is instantly, they loved each other.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"मगर ज़मीन की एक राजकुमारी और पानी का एक राजकुमार — दोनों की ही दुनियाओं को इस बात पर ऐतराज़ था। उसके अपने लोग चाहते थे कि वह नीचे ही रहे। और राजकुमारी के लोग यह समझ ही नहीं पा रहे थे कि वह आख़िर क्या चीज़ है।","lang":"hi","body":"But a princess of the land and a prince of the water — both their worlds had opinions about that. His people wanted him below. Hers could not understand what he was.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"कुछ समय के लिए — और इस कहानी में हम यही हिस्सा सुना रहे हैं — वे दोनों बस बेहद खुश रहे। उसने राजकुमारी को झरने के नीचे दीयों से जगमगाते कमरे दिखाए, जहाँ की दीवारें किसी सीप के अंदरूनी हिस्से की तरह चमकती थीं। और राजकुमारी ने उसे खुबानी के फूल दिखाए, बर्फ़ दिखाई, और महसूस कराया कि ताज़ी रोटी की खुशबू कैसी होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"For a time — and this is the part of the tale this telling keeps — they were simply happy. He showed her the lamplit rooms below the spring, where the walls glimmered like the inside of a shell. She showed him apricot blossom, and snow, and how bread smells.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.himal-nagrai-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.himal-nagrai:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Himal and the Serpent Prince","text":"पूरी कहानी, जो दादियाँ सर्दियों की कई-कई रातों में सुनाती हैं, इससे बहुत आगे तक जाती है — जलन, भूल-चूक और एक लंबे अफ़सोस से गुज़रती हुई — क्योंकि आख़िरकार, यह दुनिया की सबसे दर्दभरी कहानियों में से एक है, और कश्मीर भी इसे झुठलाने की कोशिश नहीं करता।","lang":"hi","body":"The full tale, the one grandmothers tell over many winter nights, goes on far past this — through jealousy and mistakes and long sorrow — for it is, in the end, one of the world's great sad stories, and Kashmir does not pretend otherwise.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-himal-nagrai.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.himal-nagrai|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"लगभग सात सौ साल पहले, कश्मीर की घाटी में लल्ला नाम की एक स्त्री रहती थीं। कम उम्र में ही उनका ब्याह एक ऐसे घर में कर दिया गया था जहाँ लोग उनके साथ बहुत बेरहमी से पेश आते थे, और एक दिन — सभी कहानियाँ इस बात पर एकमत हैं — वह ईश्वर की खोज में उस पूरी ज़िंदगी को हमेशा के लिए पीछे छोड़ कर निकल पड़ीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Around seven hundred years ago, in the Kashmir valley, there lived a woman called Lalla. She had been married young into a house that was unkind to her, and one day — the tellings agree on this — she walked out of that life entirely, to seek God.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"वह अपनी बाकी की ज़िंदगी उस घाटी में घूमती रहीं, न उनके पास कोई धन-दौलत थी, न किसी बात का डर। और चलते-चलते वह कविताएँ कहती जाती थीं — कश्मीरी में छोटी, असरदार रचनाएँ, बस चंद पंक्तियों की, जिन्हें 'वाख' कहा जाता है। यानी वचन।","lang":"hi","body":"She wandered the valley for the rest of her days, owning nothing, fearing nothing. And as she walked, she spoke poems — short, sharp verses in Kashmiri, each one a handful of lines, called vakhs. Sayings.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"\"ये वाख ऐसे थे जैसे किसी ने पहले कभी न सुने हों। उनमें कहा गया था कि ईश्वर किसी मंदिर या किताब में दूर नहीं, बल्कि पास हैं — अपनी सांस से भी ज़्यादा पास — और ईश्वर को पाने का मतलब है पूरी ईमानदारी से, हर दिखावे से परे अपने अंदर झांकना। जिसने भी एक बार कोई वाख सुना, वह उसे फिर कभी भूल नहीं पाया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The vakhs were unlike anything anyone had heard. They said that God was not far away in some temple or some book, but near — nearer than your own breath — and that finding God meant looking inward, honestly, past every pretence. People heard one and could not forget it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"\"किसी के इन्हें लिखने से पहले सैकड़ों सालों तक ये पद गीतों की तरह फैलते रहे — ज़ुबान से ज़ुबान, माँ से बच्चे और गड़ेरिए से गड़ेरिए तक। आज भी कश्मीरी लोग बातचीत में ऐसे कोई वाख कह देते हैं जैसे बाकी लोग कोई कहावत बोलते हैं, और हर कोई हामी में सिर हिलाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The verses spread the way songs spread — from mouth to mouth, mother to child, shepherd to shepherd — for hundreds of years before anyone wrote them down. To this day, Kashmiris drop a vakh into conversation the way others quote a proverb, and everyone nods.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"\"और फिर एक बड़ी प्यारी बहस भी है। कश्मीरी हिंदू उन्हें अपनी परंपरा की महान संत लल्लेश्वरी मानकर पूजते हैं। कश्मीरी मुसलमान उन्हें अपनी परंपरा की महान फ़क़ीर लल्ला आरिफ़ा के रूप में सम्मान देते हैं। दोनों ही उनकी कहानियाँ संजोए हैं। दोनों ही उनके पद दोहराते हैं। वह किसकी हैं?\"","lang":"hi","body":"And then there is the beautiful argument. Kashmiri Hindus revere her as Lalleshwari, a great saint of their tradition. Kashmiri Muslims revere her as Lalla Arifa, a great mystic of theirs. Both keep her stories. Both quote her verses. Whose is she?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"\"उनके इर्द-गिर्द वैसे ही किस्से-कहानियाँ पनप गईं जैसे चिनार पर काई जमती है — ऐसी कहानियाँ कि कैसे उन्होंने गुरुओं को हैरान कर दिया और एक सीधे-सादे वाक्य से घमंडी लोगों का घमंड तोड़ दिया। कहानियाँ भले अलग हों, पर इन पदों को उनकी ज़रूरत नहीं है। ये पद ही असली चमत्कार हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Legends grew around her the way moss grows on a chinar — tales of teachers she astonished and proud men she deflated with one plain sentence. The legends differ; the verses do not need them. The verses are the miracle.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lal-ded-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lal-ded:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Woman Everyone Claims","text":"\"विद्वान आपको पूरी संजीदगी से बताएंगे: कश्मीरी साहित्य की शुरुआत उन्हीं से होती है। इस भाषा की जो सबसे पुरानी कविता हम तक पहुँची है, वह लल्ला की ही देन है — एक ऐसी घुमक्कड़ स्त्री जिनके पास अपना कुछ नहीं था, पर जो इस घाटी के लिए सबसे अनमोल विरासतों में से एक छोड़ गईं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Scholars will tell you soberly: she is the beginning of Kashmiri literature itself. The oldest poetry in the language that came down to us comes from Lalla — a wandering woman who owned nothing and left one of the richest inheritances in the valley.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lal-ded.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lal-ded|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"श्रीनगर की डल झील पर सूरज उगने से पहले, पानी चारों तरफ खड़े पहाड़ों के बीच स्लेटी रेशम की चादर जैसा लगता है — और अंधेरे में से, हर दिशा से नावें निकलकर आने लगती हैं। लकड़ी की लंबी और पतली नावें जिन्हें शिकारा कहते हैं, दिल के आकार वाले चप्पुओं से चलाई जाती हैं और ऊपर तक सब्ज़ियों से लदी होती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Before sunrise on Dal Lake, in Srinagar, the water is a sheet of grey silk with mountains standing round it — and out of the dark, from every direction, come boats. Long, slim wooden boats called shikaras, paddled with heart-shaped oars, loaded to the gunwales with vegetables.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"वे झील के ठीक बीचों-बीच मिलती हैं, और वहीं — बिना किसी दुकान, सड़क या सूखी ज़मीन के — बाज़ार सज जाता है। नावें एक-दूसरे से सटकर जुड़ जाती हैं; पानी के ऊपर ही टमाटर, साग-सब्ज़ी, कमल ककड़ी और ताज़ी रोटियाँ एक हाथ से दूसरे हाथ जाती हैं; और कश्मीरी में बड़े जोश के साथ मोल-भाव चलता है।","lang":"hi","body":"They meet in the middle of the lake, and there — with no shop, no street, no dry land anywhere in sight — the market opens. Boats raft up side by side; tomatoes, greens, lotus stems and fresh bread change hands over the water; the haggling is in Kashmiri and it is enthusiastic.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"जब तक सूरज पहाड़ों के ऊपर आता है, बाज़ार खत्म हो चुका होता है। नावें बिखर जाती हैं, रेशमी पानी फिर शांत हो जाता है, और देर से जागने वाला कोई सैलानी कभी अंदाज़ा भी नहीं लगा पाएगा कि झील पर सुबह-सुबह का पूरा कारोबार निपट भी चुका है।","lang":"hi","body":"By the time the sun clears the mountains, it is over. The boats scatter, the silk smooths out, and a visitor waking late would never guess the lake had already done a whole morning's business.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"क्योंकि डल सिर्फ देखने भर की कोई झील नहीं है — यह तो एक पूरा मोहल्ला है। लोग इस पर और इसके इर्द-गिर्द रहते हैं: पगडंडियों और विलो के पेड़ों वाले तैरते हुए पूरे गाँव, खुद चप्पू चलाकर स्कूल जाते बच्चे, और शिकारे पर बैठकर अपनी डाक बाँटता डाकिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Because Dal is not just a lake to look at — it is a neighbourhood. People live on it and around it: whole floating villages of walkways and willows, children paddling themselves to school, a postman doing his round by shikara.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"यहाँ के बाग़-बगीचे भी तैरते हैं। किसान सरकंडों और झील की घास से क्यारियाँ बुनते हैं, उन पर झील की उपजाऊ मिट्टी बिछाते हैं, और तैरते हुए तख्तों पर सब्ज़ियाँ उगाते हैं — ऐसे बाग़ जिन्हें खींचकर कहीं भी ले जाया जा सकता है। एक दादाजी ने घूमने आए अपने पोते को यह बात बताई, जिसे तब तक एक भी बात का यकीन नहीं हुआ जब तक कि वह खुद ऐसे एक बाग़ पर खड़ा नहीं हो गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The gardens float too. Farmers weave beds of reeds and lake-weed, spread them with rich lake mud, and grow vegetables on rafts — gardens you can tow. A grandfather explained it to his visiting grandson, who did not believe a word until he stood on one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"और फिर हाउसबोट भी हैं — नक्काशीदार लकड़ी के लंबे घर जो अपने खूंटों से बंधे पानी पर तैरते रहते हैं, जिनमें बैठकें, फूलों वाले परदे और शान से लिखे नाम होते हैं। यह सिलसिला पीढ़ियों पुराना है: बहुत पहले जो सैलानी ज़मीन पर घर नहीं बना सकते थे, उन्होंने पानी पर घर बना लिए, और कश्मीरी कारीगरों ने उन्हें बेहद खूबसूरत बना दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"And then there are the houseboats — long carved wooden houses that ride at their moorings, with sitting rooms and flowered curtains and names painted in proud letters. The tradition goes back generations: visitors long ago who could not build houses on the land built them on the water instead, and Kashmiri craftsmen made them beautiful.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dal-morning-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dal-morning:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lake That Is a Neighbourhood","text":"झील की अपनी परेशानियाँ हैं — सालों में यह सिकुड़ती चली गई है, जंगली घास और गंदगी ने इसे जकड़ रखा है, और बहुत से लोग इसे साफ़ करने और बचाने में जुटे हैं, क्योंकि ऐसा अनूठा आस-पड़ोस दोबारा नहीं मिल सकता।","lang":"hi","body":"The lake has its worries — it has shrunk over the years, and weeds and dirt press it hard, and many people work to clean and protect it, because a neighbourhood this rare cannot be replaced.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dal-morning.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dal-morning|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"कश्मीरी में इसे बून कहते हैं; किताबों में, चिनार। यह प्लेन प्रजाति का पेड़ है, और कश्मीर में यह इतना विशाल हो जाता है कि देखे बिना यक़ीन ही न हो — तने कमरे से भी ज़्यादा चौड़े, हरी घटा जैसी छतरी, और कुछ पेड़ तो इतने पुराने हैं कि जब वे नन्हे पौधे थे, तब शायद मुग़ल बादशाह भी उनके नीचे बैठे होंगे।","lang":"hi","body":"In Kashmiri it is called the boon; in books, the chinar. It is a plane tree, and in Kashmir it grows to a size that has to be seen to be believed — trunks wider than a room, crowns like green weather, some trees so old that Mughal emperors may have sat under them as saplings.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"ये बड़े-बड़े पेड़ सदियों पहले सोच-समझकर लगाए गए थे — मुग़ल बाग़ों के किनारे, दरगाहों के इर्द-गिर्द, गाँव के मैदानों में और झीलों के टापुओं पर — क्योंकि हर कोई एक बात पर राज़ी था: अगले पाँच सौ सालों में लोग जहाँ भी जुटें, उनके सिर पर एक चिनार ज़रूर होना चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"The great ones were planted on purpose, centuries ago — along the Mughal gardens, around shrines, on village greens and island corners of the lakes — because everyone agreed on one thing: wherever people would gather for the next five hundred years, there should be a chinar over them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"बसंत में यह पेड़ ताज़े, नए हरे पत्तों से खिल उठता है। पूरी गर्मियों में यह गाँव का सबसे बड़ा कमरा बन जाता है — ताश खेलने, ऊन कातने, गपशप लड़ाने, होमवर्क करने और झपकी लेने के लिए ठंडी छाँव, और ऊपर डालियों पर फ़ाख़्ताएँ अपने काम में लगी रहती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"In spring the tree unfolds a fresh young green. All summer it is the village's largest room — shade for card games, wool-spinning, gossip, homework and naps, with the doves conducting their business upstairs.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"और फिर आता है पतझड़, और चिनार वही करता है जिसके लिए वह मशहूर है: बिना जले आग पकड़ लेना। पहले सुनहरा, फिर चमकीला नारंगी, और फिर गहरा दहकता हुआ लाल — एक ही पेड़ पर ये तीनों रंग एक साथ दिख जाते हैं, और चिनारों की पूरी सड़क राहगीरों के क़दम और दिल दोनों थाम लेती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And then comes autumn, and the chinar does the thing it is famous for: it catches fire without burning. Gold first, then amber, then a deep blazing crimson — a single tree can hold all three at once, and a whole avenue of them stops traffic and hearts alike.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"बच्चे गिरे हुए पत्ते बटोरते हैं — पाँच कोनों वाले, फैली हुई हथेली जितने बड़े — और जिस किसी के पास भी किताब होती है, उसने पन्नों के बीच एक पत्ता दबाकर ज़रूर रखा होता है। इन सूखे पत्तों के कुछ और पुराने काम भी हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Children gather the fallen leaves — five-pointed, big as a spread hand — and everyone with a book has pressed one flat between the pages. The dry leaves have older uses too.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"फिर आती है सर्दी: बर्फ़ के बीच वह विशाल पेड़ बिना पत्तों के काला और रूपहला खड़ा रहता है, जैसे स्याही से उकेरा गया हो, सुस्ताता हुआ। कश्मीरी आपको बताएँगे कि वह तब भी ख़ूबसूरत लगता है — शायद सबसे ज़्यादा तभी, जब आप उस पूरी ताक़त को देख पाते हैं जिसने उस सारी शान को सँभाल रखा है।","lang":"hi","body":"Then winter: the great tree stands bare and black-silver against the snow, drawn in ink, resting. Kashmiris will tell you it is beautiful even then — perhaps most of all then, when you can see the whole shape of the strength that holds up all that glory.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boonyi-year-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boonyi-year:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Year Under the Chinar","text":"इन पुराने विशाल पेड़ों की अब गिनती होती है और इन्हें सुरक्षित रखा जाता है, किसी स्मारक की तरह हर एक पर नंबर दर्ज है — क्योंकि जिस पेड़ को खुद को बनाने में सदियाँ लग जाती हैं, वह एक ही दोपहर में ख़त्म हो सकता है, और घाटी जानती है कि उसके पास क्या है।","lang":"hi","body":"The old giants are counted and protected now, each one numbered like a monument — because a tree that takes centuries to become itself can be lost in an afternoon, and the valley knows what it has.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boonyi-year.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boonyi-year|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"कश्मीर की सर्दी सचमुच की कड़ाके की सर्दी होती है — खिड़कियों की चौखट तक बर्फ़, बाड़े के खंभों जैसी बर्फ़ की लटकनें, और घर के अंदर भी मुँह से धुएँ की तरह निकलती साँस। इसके सबसे कठिन दौर का तो एक नाम भी है: चिल्लई कलाँ, यानी \"बड़ी ठंड\", कड़ाके की सर्दी के वे चालीस दिन जब घाटी पूरी तरह जम जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Kashmiri winter is serious winter — snow to the windowsills, icicles like fence posts, breath like smoke indoors. Its hardest stretch even has a name: Chillai Kalan, \"the great cold,\" forty days in the deep of winter when the valley truly freezes.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"इस ठंड से बचने के लिए कश्मीरियों ने बहुत पहले दो नायाब चीज़ें ईजाद की थीं। पहला है फेरन — एक लंबा, ढीला-ढाला ऊनी गाउन जो सारे कपड़ों के ऊपर पहना जाता है और लगभग टखनों तक आता है। यह इतना खुला होता है कि आप अपने दोनों हाथ पूरी तरह अंदर खींच सकते हैं और असल में, सिर निकला हुआ एक छोटा गरम तंबू बन सकते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Against it, Kashmiris long ago perfected two pieces of equipment. The first is the pheran — a long, loose woollen gown that goes on over everything and reaches nearly to the ankles, roomy enough to pull your arms inside entirely and become, in effect, a small warm tent with a head.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"दूसरा तरीका तो कमाल की सूझबूझ वाला है। कांगड़ी: दहकते अंगारों वाली मिट्टी की एक छोटी-सी हाँडी, जो हत्थेदार सुंदर बुनी हुई बेंत की टोकरी में आराम से समा जाती है। आप इसे फेरन के नीचे, अपने से सटाकर रखते हैं — आपकी अपनी, साथ चलने वाली, न दिखने वाली आग।","lang":"hi","body":"The second is the genius part. The kangri: a little clay pot of glowing embers, snug in a beautifully woven willow basket with a handle. You carry it under the pheran, held against you — your own personal, portable, invisible fire.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"कई घरों में सुबह-सुबह कांगड़ी तैयार करना एक छोटे-से नियम जैसा होता है, और यह ज़िम्मेदारी अक्सर दादी या नानी की होती है: कोयले को ठीक से बिछाना, अंगारों को सुलगाना, और ऊपर से राख की परत चढ़ाना ताकि गर्माहट घंटों बनी रहे। अगर अच्छे से तैयार की जाए, तो एक बार भरी कांगड़ी कड़ाके की ठंड में आधा दिन आराम से निकाल देती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Filling the kangri is a small morning ceremony in many houses, and it often belongs to a grandmother: charcoal laid just so, embers coaxed, ash banked over the top so the warmth will last for hours. Done well, one filling sees you through half a day of the great cold.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"बाहर से आया एक बच्चा, जो सर्दियों में अपने रिश्तेदारों के यहाँ गया था, उसने देखा कि इतने ठंडे कमरे में भी सब बड़े आराम और चैन से बैठे हैं, और उसने झट से पूछा कि आखिर यह जादू क्या है।","lang":"hi","body":"A child from outside, visiting winter relatives, once watched everyone sitting comfortably in a freezing room, mysteriously content, and demanded to know the trick.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"इसके हर हिस्से में एक हुनर है: बेंत बुनने वाले कारीगर जो टोकरियाँ बनाते हैं — कुछ रोज़मर्रा के लिए सादी, तो कुछ तोहफ़ों के लिए सुंदर और रंग-बिरंगी — और इसे बरतने का सलीका भी, क्योंकि कांगड़ी को बड़ी इज़्ज़त और हिफ़ाज़त से संभाला जाता है, जैसा आग रखने वाली हर चीज़ के साथ होना चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"There is craft in every part of it: the willow-weavers who make the baskets — some plain for every day, some patterned and bright for gifts — and the etiquette of it, because a kangri must be handled with respect and care, as anything holding fire must.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kangri-winter-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kangri-winter:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fire You Can Carry","text":"अब इसमें सर्दियों का नाश्ता भी जोड़ लीजिए — गुलाब के रंग जैसी भाप उड़ाती नमकीन चाय, सुबह-सुबह बेकरी से आई ताज़ा रोटी, और सबसे ठंडी सुबहों में गरमा-गरम हरीसा — तो चिल्लई कलाँ दुश्मन नहीं, बल्कि ऐसा मौसम लगने लगता है जिसके लिए ही यह पूरा रिवाज़ बना हो।","lang":"hi","body":"Add the winter table — steaming salt tea the colour of a rose, fresh bread from the baker's morning batch, harissa on the coldest mornings — and Chillai Kalan starts to look less like an enemy and more like the season the whole culture was designed for.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kangri-winter.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kangri-winter|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Valley and the Lake"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"हरियाणा के हिसार ज़िले में राखीगढ़ी नाम का एक किसानी गाँव है — भैंसें, गेहूँ के खेत, ईंटों के मकान और वही आम सा मौसम। और उसके पास और उसके नीचे दबे हैं धूल भरे बड़े-बड़े टीले, जहाँ बच्चे हमेशा से पतंग उड़ाते और बकरियाँ चराते आए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"In Hisar district of Haryana there is a farming village called Rakhigarhi — buffaloes, wheat, brick houses, the usual weather. And beside and beneath it, a set of great dusty mounds, where children have always flown kites and grazed goats.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"गाँव वालों को हमेशा से पता था कि ये टीले कुछ अजीब हैं। हलों से टकराकर मिट्टी के बहुत पुराने बर्तनों के अजीबोगरीब टुकड़े निकल आते। बारिश के बाद ज़मीन से मोती बाहर निकल आते — छोटे-छोटे, सलीके से गढ़े हुए, छेददार मोती, जैसे किसी दुकान पर नहीं मिलते थे। लोग कंधे उचकाते, सुंदर मोतियों को जेब में रख लेते और वापस खेती-किसानी में लग जाते।","lang":"hi","body":"The village always knew the mounds were strange. Ploughs turned up odd bits of very old pottery. After rain, the ground offered up beads — tiny, neat, drilled beads of a kind no shop sold. People shrugged, pocketed the pretty ones, and got on with farming.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"फिर अपने ब्रश और अपने सब्र के साथ पुरातत्वविद आए, और बड़े ध्यान से, एक-एक चौकोर खाने को बड़ी आहिस्ता-आहिस्ता खोलते हुए, उन्होंने उन टीलों को खंगालना शुरू किया।","lang":"hi","body":"Then the archaeologists came, with their brushes and their patience, and began — very slowly, square by careful square — to take the mounds apart.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"और कोई ऐसा-वैसा शहर नहीं। जैसे-जैसे खुदाई आगे बढ़ी, राखीगढ़ी एक बहुत ही विशाल शहर निकला — अब तक मिले हड़प्पा सभ्यता के सबसे बड़े शहरों में से एक, मशहूर मोहनजोदड़ो और हड़प्पा के ही परिवार का, और क्षेत्रफल में उनमें से ज़्यादातर से भी बड़ा।","lang":"hi","body":"And not just any city. As the digging spread, Rakhigarhi turned out to be enormous — one of the largest Harappan cities ever found, in the same family as the famous Mohenjo-daro and Harappa, and bigger in area than most of them.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"धरती के भीतर से पचास सदियों पहले के लोगों की रोज़मर्रा की ज़िंदगी बाहर निकल आई: सीधी गलियों के किनारे बने कच्ची ईंटों के घर, चूल्हे, अनाज रखने के बड़े-बड़े मटके, मिट्टी के नन्हे पहियों वाली खिलौना गाड़ियाँ, चूड़ियाँ और हज़ारों की तादाद में वही मोती — क्योंकि राखीगढ़ी मोती बनाने का एक बहुत बड़ा केंद्र रहा था, और लगता है कि उसके कारख़ाने दूर-दूर तक मशहूर थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Out of the earth came the everyday life of people from fifty centuries ago: mud-brick houses along straight lanes, kitchen hearths, storage jars, toy carts with little clay wheels, bangles, and thousands of those beads — for Rakhigarhi had been a great bead-making town, its workshops famous, it seems, far and wide.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"ज़रा सोचिए कि उन खिलौना गाड़ियों का क्या मतलब है: पाँच हज़ार साल पहले, ठीक इसी ज़मीन पर, बच्चे खिलौना बैलगाड़ियों से खेलते थे — जबकि खुदाई के खंदकों के ठीक बाहर, आज के राखीगढ़ी की असली बैलगाड़ियाँ चरमराहट के साथ गुज़र रही थीं। खुद पुरातत्वविदों ने भी इस बात पर हैरत जताई।","lang":"hi","body":"Think what the toy carts mean: five thousand years ago, on this exact ground, children played with toy bullock carts — while outside the trench, present-day Rakhigarhi's actual bullock carts creaked past. The archaeologists themselves remarked on it.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.rakhigarhi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.rakhigarhi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Village on Top of a Lost City","text":"खुदाई मौसम-दर-मौसम चलती रहती है, और अब यह गाँव भी इसका हिस्सा बन चुका है — स्थानीय लोग खुद इस खुदाई में काम करते हैं, मिली हुई चीज़ों के लिए एक संग्रहालय बनाया गया है, और राखीगढ़ी के लोग भारत की एक महान प्राचीन जगह के मेज़बान बन गए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The digging goes on, season by season, and the village is part of it now — locals work the excavations, a museum has been built for the finds, and the people of Rakhigarhi have become hosts of one of India's great ancient places.","art":"art/story/sm/it-rakhigarhi.jpg","route":"#/story/it.rakhigarhi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"हरियाणा के हर गाँव का अपना एक जोहड़ होता है — यानी गाँव का तालाब — जहाँ भैंसें चमकते काले टापुओं की तरह पानी में डूबी रहती हैं और बगुले धीरे-धीरे पहरा देते हैं। और तालाब के पास, गाँव-गाँव में, एक और चीज़ भी होती है: अखाड़ा। यानी कुश्ती की मिट्टी।","lang":"hi","body":"Every proper Haryana village has its johad — the village pond — where the buffaloes soak like glossy black islands and the herons do their slow patrolling. And near the pond, in village after village, there is something else: the akhara. The wrestling pit.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"अखाड़ा एक खास मिट्टी का चौकोर घेरा होता है — नरम, गहरी, जिसे तब तक खोदा, समेटा और सींचा जाता है जब तक कि वह कोको पाउडर जैसी न हो जाए — और यह एक तरह से पवित्र ज़मीन होती है। पहलवान इसमें कदम रखने से पहले इसे माथे से लगाते हैं। इसमें जूते पहनकर नहीं जाते। इसमें थूकते नहीं हैं। कभी भी नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The akhara is a square of special earth — soft, deep, turned and raked and watered until it is like cocoa powder — and it is holy ground of a sort. Wrestlers touch it to their foreheads before they step in. You do not wear shoes in it. You do not spit in it. Ever.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"सूरज निकलने से पहले ही अखाड़ा भर जाता है। पहलवानों की कतारें मुगदर घुमाती हैं, रस्सियों पर चढ़ती हैं, और इतनी दंड-बैठक लगाती हैं कि जब तक आप खुद वहाँ खड़े होकर न गिनें, तब तक यह सिर्फ़ मनगढ़ंत बातें ही लगेंगी।","lang":"hi","body":"Before dawn, the pit fills. Rows of wrestlers — pehelwans — swing clubs, climb ropes, and do dand-baithak, push-ups and squats, in numbers that sound like made-up bragging until you stand there and count along.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"पुराने उस्ताद — जो हर अखाड़े में होते हैं — इस जगह को दो ही ईंधनों पर चलाते हैं: अनुशासन और दूध। \"कुश्ती कोई लड़ाई नहीं है,\" वे नए बच्चों से कहते हैं। \"लड़ाई गुस्सा होती है। कुश्ती तो अभ्यास, खुराक, नींद और इज़्ज़त है। इस अखाड़े का सबसे ताक़तवर इंसान वही है, जो सबसे ज़्यादा सालों तक सबसे पहले सोकर उठा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The old coach — every akhara has one — runs the place on two fuels: discipline and milk. \"Kushti is not fighting,\" he tells the new children. \"Fighting is anger. Kushti is practice, food, sleep, respect. The strongest person in this pit is the one who got up earliest for the most years.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"बहुत, बहुत लंबे समय तक अखाड़ा सिर्फ़ लड़कों के लिए ही था। फिर, अभी कुछ ही साल पहले, हरियाणा में लड़कियाँ भी अखाड़ों में उतरने लगीं — और पूरे ज़िले की त्योरियों के बावजूद कुछ पिताओं और कोचों ने उनका साथ दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"For a long, long time, the pit was only for boys. Then, not so many years ago, girls in Haryana began stepping into the akharas too — and some fathers and coaches backed them against every frown in the district.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"यह छोटा-सा राज्य अब भारत के कुश्ती और मुक्केबाज़ी के पदकों का एक बड़ा हिस्सा जीतता है, और हर किसी की अपनी राय है — यहाँ का दूध, घी, हवा, या यहाँ की ज़िद। कोच मुस्कुराते हैं और अखाड़े की ओर इशारा करते हैं: यह बरसों-बरस सुबह जल्दी उठने की बात है।","lang":"hi","body":"This little state now produces an outsized share of India's wrestling and boxing medals, and everyone has a theory — the milk, the ghee, the air, the stubbornness. The coaches smile and point at the pit: it is the getting up early, for the most years.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.akhara-pond-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.akhara-pond:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wrestlers by the Village Pond","text":"और जब कोई दंगल होता है — यानी कुश्ती का मुकाबला — तो पूरा इलाका उमड़ पड़ता है। खुले में मिट्टी पर दाँव-पेंच, लाउडस्पीकर, गन्ने बेचने वाले, दाँव-पेचों पर अपनी पक्की राय रखने वाली दादियाँ, और सबसे आगे की कतार में बैठकर अपने भविष्य का फ़ैसला करते छोटे-छोटे बच्चे।","lang":"hi","body":"And when a dangal is held — a tournament — the whole countryside comes. Bouts on the earth in the open, loudspeakers, sugarcane sellers, grandmothers with strong opinions about technique, and small children in the front row, deciding their futures.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-akhara-pond.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.akhara-pond|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"दक्षिणी हरियाणा के फ़रीदाबाद में, अरावली पहाड़ियों के पुराने पथरीले कंधों पर, सीढ़ियों के एक बड़े घुमाव में बना पत्थरों का एक प्राचीन कुंड है — जिसका आकार, जैसा कि लोग हमेशा कहते आए हैं, उगते सूरज जैसा है। इसका नाम भी यही कहता है: सूरजकुंड। यानी सूरज का कुंड।","lang":"hi","body":"In Faridabad, in southern Haryana, on the rocky old shoulders of the Aravalli hills, there is an ancient stone pool built in a great curve of steps — shaped, people have always said, like the rising sun. Its name says the same: Surajkund. The pool of the sun.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"मान्यताएँ इसे तोमर वंश के एक सरदार सूरजपाल से जोड़ती हैं, जिनके बारे में कहा जाता है कि उन्होंने इसे करीब एक हज़ार साल पहले बनवाया था — बारिश का पानी सहेजने की एक जगह, जिसके सीढ़ीदार पथरीले किनारों पर धूप चाहने वाले बैठ सकें। वह पुराना कुंड आज भी वक्त की मार झेले, शांत भाव से अपने उसी घुमाव को थामे खड़ा है।","lang":"hi","body":"Tradition ties it to a chieftain of the Tomar clan, named Surajpal, who is said to have built it around a thousand years ago — a place to catch and keep the rain, with stepped stone banks where the sun-loving could sit. The old pool still holds its curve, weathered and calm.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"\"साल के ज़्यादातर दिनों में यह एक शांत सा स्मारक रहता है। और फिर फ़रवरी का महीना आता है — और इस पुराने सूरज कुंड के किनारे, दुनिया के सबसे बड़े हस्तशिल्प मेलों में से एक के दरवाज़े खुल जाते हैं: सूरजकुंड मेला।\"","lang":"hi","body":"For most of the year it is a quiet monument. And then February comes — and beside the old sun pool, one of the biggest craft fairs on Earth opens its gates: the Surajkund Mela.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"\"भारत के कोने-कोने से कारीगर यहाँ आते हैं। दक्षिण से बुनकर आते हैं, ऐसा रेशम लेकर जो पानी की तरह बहता है। जयपुर की ब्लू पॉटरी। पूर्वोत्तर का बाँस का काम। पास के ही पंजाब की फुलकारी कढ़ाई। शीशे का काम, पत्थर की नक्काशी, काँसे के बर्तन, खिलौने — गलियों की गलियाँ यह दिखाती हुईं कि हुनरमंद हाथ क्या-क्या कर सकते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Craftspeople come from every corner of India. Weavers from the south with silk that pours like water. Blue pottery from Jaipur. Bamboo work from the Northeast. Phulkari embroidery from Punjab next door. Mirror-work, stone-work, bell metal, toys — lane upon lane of hands showing what hands can do.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"\"मेले में अपने माता-पिता के साथ आई एक लड़की ने एक कुम्हार को एक मिनट से भी कम समय में चाक पर मटका बनाते देखा, और उसने उनसे पूछा कि यह सीखने में उन्हें कितना समय लगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A girl at the mela with her parents watched a potter throw a pot in under a minute and asked him how long it took to learn to do that.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"\"यहाँ हर जगह का खाना है, हर साल किसी अलग राज्य के लोक नर्तक और ढोल बजाने वाले हैं, इन सबके ऊपर घूमता एक बड़ा सा झूला है — और शाम होते-होते, अपने हाथों में मिट्टी की चिड़िया, बुना हुआ थैला या छोटी सी दरी लिए बाहर निकलते परिवार हैं, मानो हर कोई किसी के सौ सालों की मेहनत अपने घर ले जा रहा हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"There is food from everywhere, folk dancers and drummers from a different featured state each year, a great wheel turning over it all — and by evening, families walking out with a clay bird, a woven bag, a small carpet, each one carrying somebody's hundred years home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.surajkund-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.surajkund:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Pool Where India Comes to Sell Wonders","text":"\"और सूरज कुंड की पुरानी पत्थरों वाली सीढ़ियाँ एक बार फिर काम में आने लगती हैं — बैठने की जगह की तरह। हज़ार साल पुराने उस घेरे पर बैठकर भीड़ नीचे नाचने वालों को देखती है, जिसे देखकर इसे बनाने वालों को शायद बहुत ख़ुशी होती: उन्होंने पानी के किनारे लोगों के जुटने की जगह बनाई थी, और लोग आज भी वहाँ जुट रहे हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the old stone steps of the sun pool get used again — as seats. Crowds settle on the thousand-year-old curve to watch the dancers below, which would probably please the builders: they made a place for people to gather by water, and people are still gathering.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-surajkund.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.surajkund|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"हरियाणा के गेहूँ और सरसों के खेतों के बीच उत्तर की ओर बढ़िए, तो एक ऐसा नाम सामने आता है जिसे सुनते ही पूरा महाभारत मानो चौंककर खड़ा हो जाता है: कुरुक्षेत्र। देखने में साधारण पर असल में बेहद अनोखा यह भूभाग वही जगह है, जहाँ परंपरा के अनुसार इस महाकाव्य का सबसे बड़ा मोड़ आया था — और इसके अलावा भी बहुत कुछ हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"Drive north through Haryana's wheat and mustard and you come to a name that makes the whole Mahabharata sit up: Kurukshetra. This ordinary-looking, extraordinary stretch of land is where tradition places the epic's great turning — and much more besides.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"पुराने ग्रंथ इस पूरे इलाके को धर्मक्षेत्र कहते हैं — यानी धर्म और सही रास्ते पर चलने की भूमि — और बताते हैं कि यह इस महागाथा से भी बहुत पहले से पावन रहा है: ऋषियों, यज्ञों और पवित्र सरोवरों की धरती, जहाँ युगों-युगों की प्रार्थनाएँ मिट्टी में रची-बसी थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The old texts call this whole region Dharmakshetra — the field of dharma, of doing right — and say it was hallowed long before the epic: a land of sages, sacrifices, and sacred waters, where prayers had soaked into the ground for ages.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"यहाँ के सरोवर आज भी इसकी शान हैं। कुरुक्षेत्र के दिल में बसा है ब्रह्म सरोवर — एक ऐसा पावन कुंड, जो इतना विशाल है कि शांत चौकोर समंदर जैसा लगता है, जिसके चारों तरफ़ नीचे उतरती सीढ़ियाँ हैं और त्योहारों के समय इस पर इतने दीये तैराए जाते हैं कि पानी छोटी-छोटी लपटों का आसमान बन जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The waters are still its glory. At the heart of Kurukshetra lies the Brahma Sarovar — a sacred pool so vast it feels like a calm square sea, with steps going down on every side and lamps floated on it at festival time until the water is a sky of small fires.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"पास ही सन्निहित सरोवर है, जिसके बारे में मान्यता है कि कुछ ख़ास मौक़ों पर सारे पावन जल यहाँ आकर मिलते हैं। और सूर्य ग्रहण के दिनों में यहाँ लाखों तीर्थयात्री स्नान करने आते हैं — क्योंकि एक पुरानी मान्यता है कि ग्रहण के समय कुरुक्षेत्र में स्नान करने से एक साथ सारे तीर्थों का पुण्य मिल जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Nearby lies the Sannihit Sarovar, where tradition says all the sacred waters gather and meet at certain times. And on days of solar eclipse, lakhs of pilgrims come to bathe here — for an old belief holds that at eclipse, bathing at Kurukshetra carries the merit of all tirthas at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"और फिर इन सबमें सबसे शांत और सबसे प्रभावशाली जगह आती है: पुराने सरोवर के किनारे स्थित ज्योतिसर, जहाँ एक बरगद का पेड़ खड़ा है। परंपरा मानती है कि इसी बरगद के पूर्वज के नीचे — और कुछ के अनुसार ठीक इसी पेड़ के नीचे — श्रीकृष्ण ने अर्जुन को भगवद्गीता सुनाई थी।","lang":"hi","body":"And then there is the quietest, mightiest spot of all: Jyotisar, on the old pool's edge, where a banyan tree stands. Tradition holds that under this banyan's ancestor — some say this very tree — Krishna spoke the Bhagavad Gita to Arjuna.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"उस पेड़ के नीचे जो कहा गया, उस पर पूरे के पूरे पुस्तकालय लिखे जा चुके हैं, और दुनिया भर के लोग आज भी इसे तब पढ़ते हैं जब ज़िंदगी के किसी मोड़ पर उनका दिल डगमगाने लगता है। दुनिया की यह सबसे ज़्यादा पढ़ी जाने वाली बातचीत हरियाणा के एक खेत में, एक बरगद के नीचे हुई — यह बात बिल्कुल सही लगती है: आख़िर भारत में ज्ञान को पेड़ों की छाँव में बैठना ही तो पसंद है।","lang":"hi","body":"Whole libraries have been written about what was said under that tree, and people across the world still read it when their own hearts fail them at some crossing. That the world's most-read conversation is placed in a Haryana field, under a banyan, feels exactly right: wisdom, in India, likes to sit under trees.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kurukshetra-waters-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kurukshetra-waters:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Land Where the Gita Was Spoken","text":"\"आज भी कुरुक्षेत्र ने यह सब कुछ सहेज रखा है — बड़े-बड़े सरोवर, ज्योतिसर का बरगद, मंदिर, और हर सर्दियों में दीयों से जगमगाते सरोवरों वाला गीता महोत्सव — और इसके चारों तरफ़, हर ओर, गेहूं की फ़सल लहलहाती रहती है, जैसा कि होना ही चाहिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Today Kurukshetra keeps it all together — the great pools, the banyan at Jyotisar, temples, a Gita festival each winter with the pools full of lamps — and around it, on every side, the wheat goes on growing, as it should.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kurukshetra-waters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kurukshetra-waters|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"\"यह किस्सा हरियाणा के गांवों में सुनाया जाता है, जहां कभी बैलों की एक अच्छी जोड़ी ही किसी परिवार का ट्रैक्टर, ट्रक और शान—सब कुछ हुआ करती थी, और जहां मेले के वक्त बैलगाड़ी की दौड़ पूरे जिले में साल भर तक चर्चा और बहस का मुद्दा बनी रह सकती थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"They tell this one in the villages of Haryana, where a good pair of bullocks was once a family's tractor, truck and pride all in one, and where a bullock-cart race at fair time could keep the district in arguments for a year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"\"एक किसान — उन्हें चौधरी रामफल कह लीजिए, सब यही कहते हैं — पशु मेले से बैलों की एक शानदार नई जोड़ी लेकर घर लौटे: जवान, ऊंचे-पूरे, ताज़े दूध जैसे सफेद, रंगे हुए सींगों और पीतल की घंटियों वाले। वे उन्हें गांव के बीच से दो बार धीरे-धीरे लेकर निकले, ताकि कोई उन्हें देखने से चूक न जाए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A farmer — call him Chaudhary Ramphal, everyone does — came home from the cattle fair with a magnificent new pair: young, tall, white as fresh milk, with painted horns and brass bells. He drove them through the village twice, slowly, to make sure nobody missed them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"\"उनके पड़ोसी, बूढ़े हुकम सिंह के पास वही पुरानी जोड़ी थी जिसे वे बारह सालों से जोत रहे थे — सलेटी, शांत, बिना किसी हड़बड़ी वाली, और दोनों में से एक का सींग मुड़ा हुआ। \\\"बढ़िया जानवर हैं,\\\" उन्होंने धीमे से कहा। \\\"मेरे वाले तो बस दो ही बातें जानते हैं। मगर कायदे से जानते हैं।\\\" रामफल ने, ज़ाहिर है, वहीं के वहीं दौड़ लगाने की चुनौती दे डाली।\"","lang":"hi","body":"His neighbour, old Hukum Singh, had the same pair he had worked for twelve years — grey, quiet, unhurried, with one bent horn between them. \"Fine animals,\" he said mildly. \"Mine only know two things. But they know them properly.\" Ramphal, of course, proposed a race on the spot.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"\"दौड़ के दिन तीन गांवों की भीड़ उमड़ पड़ी। रास्ता तय था: तालाब के किनारे-किनारे, दूर वाले बरगद का चक्कर काटकर, वापस कुएं तक। गाड़ियां चमकाई गईं। घंटियां चमकाई गईं। छोटे लड़कों को अच्छा नज़ारा देखने के लिए पेड़ों पर चढ़ाया गया, पेड़ों से उतारा गया, और फिर चढ़ाया गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Race day pulled in three villages. The course: out along the pond, around the far banyan, and back to the well. Carts polished. Bells shined. Small boys placed in trees for a better view, and removed from trees, and placed again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"पगड़ी गिरते ही सब छूटे — और रामफल की सफ़ेद जोड़ी हवा की तरह भागी। तालाब तक आते-आते वे दस गाड़ी आगे निकल चुके थे। रामफल गाड़ी में खड़ा होकर भीड़ की तरफ़ हाथ हिलाने लगा, जो किसी भी कहानी में हमेशा वही पल होता है जब चिंता शुरू हो जानी चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"At the drop of the pagri they were off — and Ramphal's white pair went like the wind. By the pond they were ten lengths ahead. Ramphal stood up in the cart waving to the crowd, which is always, in any story, the moment to start worrying.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"क्योंकि उस जवान जोड़ी में तेज़ी तो थी, लेकिन रास्ता दूर वाले बरगद के पास मुड़ता था — और सरपट दौड़ती बैलगाड़ी को मोड़ना तेज़ी का काम बिल्कुल नहीं होता।","lang":"hi","body":"Because the young pair had speed, but the far banyan is where the course turns — and turning a galloping bullock cart is not about speed at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"और पीछे-पीछे आए हुकम सिंह के बूढ़े सलेटी बैल — धीरे-धीरे, दोपहर की परछाईं की तरह सधे हुए — बरगद का मोड़ ऐसे काटा जैसे सुई में धागा पिरोया जाता है, क्योंकि उन्होंने बारह सालों में दस हज़ार मोड़ काटे थे, और अपनी ही चाल में चलते हुए, सबसे पहले कुएँ पर पहुँचे।","lang":"hi","body":"And along came Hukum Singh's old greys — dheere, dheere, steady as the noon shadow — took the banyan turn like thread going through a needle, because they had turned ten thousand corners in twelve years, and came home to the well at their own pace, first.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bail-race-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bail-race:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race of the Two Bullock Carts","text":"रामफल ने सरसों का हर्जाना भरा, जो सबको सबसे मज़ेदार बात लगी, और पूरी भीड़ को गन्ने का रस पिलाया। उसने सफ़ेद जोड़ी को अपने पास ही रखा — बारह साल तक मोड़ काटते-काटते वे भी बहुत बढ़िया निकले। और उसके बाद वह चलती गाड़ी में कभी खड़ा नहीं हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"Ramphal paid for the mustard, which everyone agreed was the funniest part, and stood the whole crowd sugarcane juice. He kept the white pair — they turned out fine, once they had done their twelve years of corners. And he never stood up in a moving cart again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bail-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bail-race|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"शाम को, जब भैंसों का दूध दुह लिया जाता है और औज़ार खूँटी पर टांग दिए जाते हैं, तब चारपाइयाँ बाहर निकलती हैं — उत्तर भारत की लकड़ी और रस्सी वाली खाट — और खुले में, बड़े बरगद के नीचे या किसी की बैठक के बाहर, एक दोस्ताना गोल घेरे में बिछा दी जाती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"In the evening, when the buffaloes have been milked and the tools hung up, the charpais come out — the wooden-framed rope cots of the north — and are set down in the open, under the big banyan or beside somebody's gate, in a rough friendly circle.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"यह है गाँव की बैठक — जहाँ सब आकर बैठते हैं। बड़े-बुजुर्ग खाटों पर जगह लेते हैं, बीच में एक पुराना हुक्का पीढ़ियों से चले आ रहे अंदाज़ में धीरे-धीरे गुड़गुड़ाता हुआ घेरे में घूमता है, और बातें शुरू हो जाती हैं। यह सिलसिला तब तक खत्म नहीं होगा, जब तक आसमान में तारे पूरी तरह से निकल न आएँ।","lang":"hi","body":"This is the village baithak — the sitting. The elders take the cots, in the middle an old hookah gurgles its way slowly around their circle as it has for generations, and the talk begins. It will not end until the stars are properly out.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"और बातें भी कैसी-कैसी! गेहूँ के भाव। किसके बेटे को सरकारी नौकरी मिली। आने वाली कोई शादी। देर से आती बारिश, जिस पर ऐसे चर्चा होती है मानो मंत्रियों की कोई गंभीर बैठक चल रही हो। और हर बात में घुला होता है मशहूर हरियाणवी मज़ाक — लू की हवा जैसा सूखा, सपाट चेहरे वाला, तीखा और एक ही साथ प्यार भरा भी।","lang":"hi","body":"And what talk it is. The price of wheat. Whose son got a government job. The wedding coming up. The rain that is late, discussed with the seriousness of a cabinet meeting. And laced through everything, the famous Haryanvi humour — dry as the loo wind, deadpan, merciless and affectionate at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"आधी बातचीत तो पीढ़ियों से तराशी हुई कहावतें और ताने होते हैं। कोई शेखी बघारता है, तो एक ही जुमले में उसकी हवा निकल जाती है। कोई रोना रोता है, तो उसे ऐसे आदमी की कहानी सुना दी जाती है जो उससे भी ज़्यादा रोता था। कोई बच नहीं पाता, और कोई बचना चाहता भी नहीं — क्योंकि इस घेरे में खिंचाई होना ही तो इस बात का सबूत है कि आप उनके अपने हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Half the talk is proverbs and taunts polished by generations. A boaster gets deflated in one line. A complainer gets a story about a man who complained more. Nobody escapes, and nobody would want to — being teased in the circle is how you know you belong to it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"और हँसी-मज़ाक के बीच, चुपके से यह बैठक बड़े-बड़े काम भी निपटा देती है। खेत की मेड़ का कोई झगड़ा छिड़ जाता है — घुमा-फिराकर, जैसे ऐसे मसले उठा करते हैं। हर कोई अपनी बात रखता है। किसी को याद आता है कि दादा-परदादाओं ने इसे कैसे सुलझाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"And quietly, between the jokes, the circle does real work. A quarrel over a field boundary comes up — sideways, as these things do. Everyone has a say. Somebody remembers how the grandfathers settled it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"बच्चों को कहने के लिए तो सोने भेज दिया जाता है, मगर वे बाहर की खाटों पर सोने का नाटक करते हुए पड़े रहते हैं और सब कुछ समेटते जाते हैं — कहानियाँ, इतिहास और मज़ाक उड़ाने की बिल्कुल सही टाइमिंग। यह एक तरह का स्कूल ही है, और सब ऐसा दिखाते हैं जैसे यह कोई स्कूल नहीं, इसीलिए तो यह इतना बढ़िया चलता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Children are technically sent to bed and actually lie on the outer cots pretending to sleep, collecting everything — the stories, the history, the exact timing of the jokes. This is a school, and everyone pretends it is not, which is why it works.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.charpai-darbar-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.charpai-darbar:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Parliament Under the Banyan","text":"देर रात, जब बैठक आखिरकार उठती है, तो गरम दूध के गिलास बांटे जाते हैं, खाटों को दीवार के सहारे खड़ा कर दिया जाता है, और बरगद सुबह तक चौपाल को अकेले अपने पास संभाल लेता है — संसद स्थगित हो गई, जो कल अपने तय समय पर फिर बैठेगी, यानी जैसे ही दिन भर का काम खत्म हो जाएगा।","lang":"hi","body":"Late, when the circle finally breaks up, glasses of hot milk go round, the cots are stood up against the walls, and the banyan keeps the square to itself till morning — the parliament adjourned, to reconvene tomorrow at the usual hour, which is whenever the work is done.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-charpai-darbar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.charpai-darbar|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"लोहड़ी की रात, पंजाब की कड़ाके की ठंड में, अलाव जल उठता है और बच्चे गाते हुए घर-घर जाते हैं — और हर बच्चे को इस गीत की पहली पंक्तियाँ याद होती हैं: सुंदर मुंदरिए, हो! तेरा कौन विचारा, हो! दुल्ला भट्टी वाला, हो! सुंदर लड़की, अरे! तुम्हारा ख़्याल कौन रखेगा? दुल्ला भट्टी रखेगा!","lang":"hi","body":"On Lohri night, in the middle of the Punjabi winter, the bonfire goes up and the children go round the houses singing — and every child knows the song's first lines: Sundar mundriye, ho! Tera kaun vichara, ho! Dulla Bhatti wala, ho! Pretty girl, hey! Who will look out for you? Dulla Bhatti will!","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"दुल्ला भट्टी सचमुच का इंसान था — बादशाह अकबर के ज़माने में, सांदल बार इलाके के भट्टी कबीले का एक पंजाबी मुसलमान। लोकगीतों में उसे बार के अपने रॉबिन हुड के रूप में याद किया जाता है: जो बादशाह के लगान वसूलने वालों के आगे कभी नहीं झुका, ग़रीबों के लिए जिसका हाथ हमेशा खुला रहा, और जो सचमुच किसी से नहीं डरता था।","lang":"hi","body":"Dulla Bhatti was real — a Punjabi Muslim of the Bhatti clan, from the Sandal Bar country, in the days of the emperor Akbar. The ballads remember him as the Bar's own Robin Hood: defiant of the emperor's tax-men, open-handed to the poor, and afraid of exactly nobody.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"यह गीत जिस कारनामे को याद दिलाता है, वह यह है। उन मुश्किल दिनों में, ऐसे दुष्ट लोग थे जो बेटियों को चुरा लेते थे — ग़रीब परिवारों की लड़कियों को ज़बरदस्ती उठा ले जाते और उन्हें बेचने के लिए ले जाते थे। उन परिवारों के पास न तो सिपाही थे और न ही सोना। उनके पास गुहार लगाने के लिए कोई रास्ता नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"The deed the song keeps is this. In those rough times, there were men wicked enough to steal daughters — to take girls from poor families by force and carry them off to be sold. The families had no soldiers and no gold. They had nowhere to turn.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"वे उस बागी की शरण में पहुँचे। दुल्ला भट्टी तक ख़बर पहुँची कि दो लड़कियों, सुंदरी और मुंदरी को — गीत की वही सुंदर मुंदरिए — उनके गाँव से उठा लिया गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"They turned to the outlaw. Word reached Dulla Bhatti of two girls, Sundri and Mundri — the sundar mundriye of the song — taken from their village.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"उसने उन्हें अपनी बेटियाँ घोषित कर दिया। अपनी खुद की बेटियाँ। बचाई गई लड़की के बारे में शायद लोग पीठ पीछे बातें करते — लेकिन दुल्ला भट्टी की बेटी के बारे में कानाफूसी करने की किसी में हिम्मत नहीं थी। और जब वक़्त आया, तो उसने सबके सामने उनका पिता बनकर खुद उनकी शादियाँ रचाईं।","lang":"hi","body":"He declared them his daughters. His. A rescued girl might still be whispered about — but nobody whispers about the daughter of Dulla Bhatti. And when it was time, he arranged their weddings himself, standing as their father in front of everyone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"उस शादी की एक-एक बात उस गीत में आज भी याद की जाती है: उस बाग़ी के पास न तो पंडित की दक्षिणा थी और न ही कोई शानदार तोहफ़े, तो जो बन पड़ा उसने वही किया — उसने आग जलाई, दुआएँ दीं, और शादी के शगुन में बच्चियों की झोली में नाप कर शक्कर डाल दी। एक पिता की मिठास, जो एक ऐसे इंसान ने दी जिसे हुकूमत मुजरिम कहती थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The song remembers the details of that wedding: the outlaw who had no priest's fee and no fine gifts did what he could — he lit a fire, said the blessings, and poured a measure of shakkar, of sugar, into the girls' laps as their wedding gift. A father's sweetness, given by a man the empire called a criminal.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"इसीलिए लोहड़ी उसी की मानी जाती है। वह अलाव, वे गीत, वे मिठाइयाँ — तिल और गुड़, और आग की लपटों में डाला जाने वाला पॉपकॉर्न — लोहड़ी की हर आग, एक तरह से, उस शादी की वही आग है जो आज भी जल रही है।","lang":"hi","body":"That is why Lohri belongs to him. The bonfire, the songs, the sweets — the til and the gud, the sesame and the jaggery, the popcorn thrown in the flames — every Lohri fire is, in a way, that wedding fire still burning.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dulla-bhatti-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dulla-bhatti:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Song Around the Lohri Fire","text":"हुकूमत के ख़िलाफ़ दुल्ला की बगावत का अंत वैसा ही हुआ जैसा ऐसी कहानियों का अक्सर होता है, किसी भी अलाव से बहुत दूर — पुराने गीतों में यह बात कही गई है, और बड़े इसे वहाँ ढूँढ सकते हैं। बच्चों का गीत उस मोड़ तक नहीं जाता, और न ही हम जाएँगे। यह गीत तो बस उस आग, उन बेटियों और उस शक्कर के साथ ही रहता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Dulla's defiance of the empire ended the way such stories usually end, far from any bonfire — the ballads tell it, and grown-ups can find it there. The children's song does not go to that place, and neither do we. The song stays with the fire, and the daughters, and the sugar.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dulla-bhatti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dulla-bhatti|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"शेख़ चिल्ली — पंजाब और हरियाणा में शेख़ चिल्ली को कौन नहीं जानता — दुनिया का सबसे बड़ा सपने देखने वाला था। उसकी जेब में कभी दो सिक्के भी खनकने को नहीं होते थे, मगर अपने दिमाग़ में वह हमेशा ठाठ-बाट से रईस रहता था। उसकी योजनाओं के अंदर भी योजनाएँ चलती थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Sheikh Chilli — everyone in Punjab and Haryana knows Sheikh Chilli — was the greatest dreamer who ever lived. He never had two coins to rub together, but inside his head he was permanently, gloriously rich. His plans had plans.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"एक दिन एक व्यापारी ने उसे सिर पर तेल का एक बड़ा मटका रखकर बाज़ार तक ले जाने की मज़दूरी दी। \"रास्ते में देर मत लगाना और ख़्याली पुलाव मत पकाना,\" व्यापारी ने कहा, जिससे यह साबित हो गया कि वह शेख़ चिल्ली से पहले कभी नहीं मिला था।","lang":"hi","body":"One day a merchant paid him to carry a big pot of oil to the market town, balanced on his head. \"Do not dawdle and do not daydream,\" said the merchant, proving he had never met Sheikh Chilli before.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"चिल्ली चल पड़ा, और दूसरे मील के पत्थर तक पहुँचते-पहुँचते सपने शुरू हो चुके थे। \"अपनी मज़दूरी से मैं अंडे ख़रीदूँगा। अंडों से निकलेंगी मुर्गियाँ। मुर्गियों से और अंडे, और फिर और मुर्गियाँ — मेरे तो घुटनों तक मुर्गियाँ ही मुर्गियाँ होंगी। मैं उन्हें बेचकर बकरियाँ ख़रीदूँगा। बकरियों से बनेंगी भैंसें। और भैंसों से बनेंगे खेत।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Chilli set off, and by the second milestone the dream had started. \"With my wages I shall buy eggs. Eggs become hens. Hens become more eggs, and more hens — I shall be up to my knees in hens. I shall sell them and buy goats. Goats become buffaloes. Buffaloes become fields.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"चौथे मील के पत्थर तक उसके पास नक्काशीदार दरवाज़ों वाली एक हवेली थी। पाँचवें तक, सपने में, सात गाँवों की सबसे समझदार और सबसे सुंदर औरत से उसकी शादी हो चुकी थी, और उनका नन्हा बेटा आँगन में डगमगाते कदमों से बाहें फैलाए उसकी तरफ़ आ रहा था — बड़ा ही प्यारा, और ज़रा सा कीचड़ में सना हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"By the fourth milestone he had a haveli with carved doors. By the fifth he was married, in the dream, to the wisest and loveliest woman in seven villages, and their little son was toddling towards him across the courtyard, arms out, adorable, slightly muddy.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"\"अरे, पर अनुशासन भी तो कोई चीज़ है!\" सपनों वाले चिल्ली ने अपने सपनों वाले बेटे से सख्ती से कहा। \"कीचड़ भरे हाथ मेरे नए कोट से दूर रखो! जब मैंने ना कह दिया, तो ना—\" और यहाँ असली शेख चिल्ली ने, असली सड़क पर, सचमुच अपना पैर ज़मीन पर पटका और ज़ोर से हाथ हिलाया, यह दिखाने के लिए कि एक अमीर आदमी कितनी सख्ती से 'ना' कहता है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Ah, but discipline!\" dream-Chilli told his dream-son sternly. \"Muddy hands off my new coat! When I say no—\" and here the real Sheikh Chilli, on the real road, gave a real stamp of his foot and a great sweep of his arm to show just how firmly a rich man says no.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"शेख चिल्ली देर तक उस पोखर को देखता खड़ा रहा। फिर वह उसके पास बैठ गया और एक-एक करके ज़ोर-ज़ोर से विलाप करने लगा: \"हाय मेरा बेटा! मेरी हवेली! मेरी भैंसें! मेरी मुर्गियाँ!\" — और इस तरह गुस्से से तमतमाता हुआ व्यापारी जब पहुँचा, तो उसने देखा कि एक आदमी खाली सड़क पर बैठकर ऐसे रिश्तेदारों के लिए रो रहा था जिन्हें सिर्फ़ वही देख सकता था।","lang":"hi","body":"Sheikh Chilli stood looking at the puddle for a long moment. Then he sat down beside it and mourned, loudly, in order: \"My son! My haveli! My buffaloes! My hens!\" — which is how the merchant, arriving furious, found a man weeping over an empty road full of relatives only he could see.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-pot-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-pot:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli Builds a Palace","text":"व्यापारी ने उसकी मज़दूरी काट ली और गुस्से में वहाँ से चला गया। गाँव वाले हफ्ते भर हँसते रहे — पर वे शेख चिल्ली के अंदाज़ में हँसे, जिसमें ज़्यादातर प्यार ही होता है, क्योंकि उनमें से हर एक ने कभी न कभी राह चलते एक-दो हवेलियाँ बनाई ही थीं, और वे यह बात जानते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The merchant docked his wages and stormed off. The village laughed for a week — but they laughed the Sheikh Chilli way, which is mostly love, because every single one of them had built a haveli or two on the road at some time, and knew it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-pot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-pot|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"शेख चिल्ली को जलाने के लिए लकड़ी चाहिए थी, और वह भी कम से कम मेहनत में—क्योंकि मेहनत तो ऐसी चीज़ थी जिसे वह किसी बड़ी मुसीबत के लिए बचाकर रखता था। उसने सड़क किनारे एक बढ़िया छायादार पेड़ चुना, एक अच्छी-मोटी डाल देखी, और दाँतों में आरी दबाकर पेड़ पर चढ़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Sheikh Chilli needed firewood, and he needed it with the least possible effort, effort being a thing he saved carefully for emergencies. He picked a fine shady tree by the road, spotted a good thick branch, and climbed up with his saw between his teeth.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"अब, आरी चलाते समय बैठा कहाँ जाए? चिल्ली ने हमेशा की तरह बड़ी गहराई से सोचा, और बैठने के लिए सबसे आरामदायक जगह चुन ली—जो कि, ज़ाहिर है, वह डाल ही थी। उस डाल का बाहरी सिरा। ठीक उस जगह के पार, जहाँ से वह उसे काट रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"Now, where to sit while sawing? Chilli considered the matter with his usual care, and chose the most comfortable seat available — which was, naturally, the branch itself. The outer end of it. On the far side of where he was cutting.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"तभी सड़क से एक मुसाफ़िर निकला। वह रुका, ऊपर देखा और आँखें झपकाईं। \"भाई,\" उसने आवाज़ दी, \"तुम तो आरी के गलत तरफ़ बैठे हो! जब वह डाल कटेगी, तो तुम भी उसके साथ ही नीचे गिरोगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Along the road came a traveller, who stopped, looked up, and blinked. \"Bhai,\" he called, \"you are sitting on the wrong side of your own sawing. When that branch comes off, you are coming with it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"शेख चिल्ली ने बड़ी दया भरी नज़रों से नीचे देखा। \"तुम्हारे पैदा होने से पहले से मैं लकड़ी काट रहा हूँ,\" उसने कहा—जो कि सरासर झूठ था—\"और आज तक किसी डाल की इतनी हिम्मत नहीं हुई कि कोई बदमाशी करे। मेहरबानी करके आप आगे बढ़िए और बढ़ई का काम बढ़ई पर ही छोड़ दीजिए।\" मुसाफ़िर ने कंधे उचकाए और चल दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Sheikh Chilli looked down with enormous pity. \"I have been cutting wood since before you were born,\" he said, which was not true, \"and no branch of mine has ever misbehaved. Kindly walk on and leave carpentry to carpenters.\" The traveller shrugged and walked on.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"चिल्ली आरी चलाता रहा। डाल से चरमराहट हुई। चिल्ली गुनगुनाते हुए आरी चलाता ही गया। डाल कड़-कड़ करके टूटी—और डाल, आरी और शेख चिल्ली, तीनों एक साथ नीचे आ गिरे! और मूर्खों पर रहने वाली खास मेहरबानी से, वह नरम घास पर धड़ाम से गिरा, पगड़ी उसकी आँखों पर आ गिरी और उसकी सारी शानो-शौकत पेड़ पर ही कहीं अटकी रह गई।","lang":"hi","body":"Chilli sawed. The branch creaked. Chilli sawed on, humming. The branch cracked — and down came branch, saw and Sheikh Chilli together, landing — by the mercy that watches over all fools — flump in the soft grass, with his turban over his eyes and his dignity somewhere up in the tree.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"उसने उस बेचारे मुसाफ़िर की आस्तीन पकड़ ली। \"हे त्रिकालदर्शी! तुमने मेरे गिरने की बात पहले ही जान ली थी! अब मुझे बाकी बातें भी बताइए—मेरा भविष्य बताइए!\" मुसाफ़िर ने उसे देखा, फिर धीरे से अपनी आस्तीन छुड़ाई। \"दोस्त, मुझे बस इतना ही दिखता है: जो जिस डाल पर बैठा है अगर उसी को काटेगा, तो ज़मीन पर ही आ गिरेगा। बस इतना ही है मेरा सारा जादू। इसे 'आँखें खोलकर देखना' कहते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He caught the poor traveller by the sleeve. \"Great knower of things! You foresaw my fall! Now tell me the rest — tell me my future!\" The traveller stared, then freed his sleeve gently. \"Friend, I foresee this much: whoever saws the branch he is sitting on will meet the ground. That is the whole of my magic. It is called looking.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sheikh-chilli-branch-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sheikh-chilli-branch:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sheikh Chilli and the Branch","text":"शेख चिल्ली बहुत प्रभावित होकर घर की ओर चल पड़े, और उन्होंने देखने की इस ज़बरदस्त कला को अपनाने की ठान ली — कल से शुरुआत करेंगे, या शायद परसों से। उनके पीछे, पूरा गाँव पहले से ही यह किस्सा एक-दूसरे को सुना रहा था और उसमें और भी मज़ेदार बातें जोड़ रहा था, और इसी तरह चार सौ सालों से उनके किस्से बढ़ते चले आ रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Sheikh Chilli walked home deeply impressed, resolving to take up this powerful art of looking — starting tomorrow, or perhaps the day after. Behind him, the village was already retelling the story, and adding better details, which is how his stories have been growing for four hundred years.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sheikh-chilli-branch.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sheikh-chilli-branch|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"\"इक सी चिड़ी, इक सी कां — एक थी चिड़िया, एक था कौआ।\" पंजाब की दादियाँ-नानियाँ इसी तरह शुरू करती हैं, और हर पंजाबी बच्चा फ़ौरन टिक कर बैठ जाता है, क्योंकि उन्हें ठीक-ठीक पता होता है कि आगे क्या आने वाला है।","lang":"hi","body":"Ik si chiri, ik si kaan — there was once a sparrow, there was once a crow. That is how the grandmothers of Punjab begin it, and every Punjabi child settles down at once, because they know exactly what is coming.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"चिड़ी को चावल का एक दाना मिला। कान को दाल का एक दाना मिला। \"साथी!\" कौवे ने बड़े ठाठ से कहा। \"हम दोनों के पास खिचड़ी बनाने का सामान है। चलो इसे पकाते हैं और मिलकर दावत उड़ाते हैं, आधा-आधा बाँटकर।\" चिड़िया, जो छोटी तो थी पर बुद्धू बिल्कुल नहीं थी, बोली, \"मिलकर का मतलब है दोनों काम करेंगे।\" \"बिल्कुल,\" कौवे ने कहा।","lang":"hi","body":"The chiri found a grain of rice. The kaan found a grain of dal. \"Partner!\" said the crow grandly. \"Between us we have the makings of khichdi. Let us cook it and feast together, share and share alike.\" The sparrow, who was small but nobody's fool, said, \"Together means both work.\"  \"Obviously,\" said the crow.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"\"पानी कौन लाएगा?\" गौरैया ने पूछा। \"मैं ले आता,\" कौए ने कहा, \"लेकिन आज मेरी चोंच में दर्द है। तुम ही ले आओ, साथी — मैं दानों की रखवाली करता हूँ।\" तो गौरैया नन्हे-नन्हे जग भर-भरकर कुएँ तक उड़ती और लौटती रही, जबकि कौआ दानों की रखवाली करता रहा — ज़्यादातर एक आरामदायक डाल पर आँखें मूँदे हुए।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Who will fetch the water?\" asked the sparrow. \"I would,\" said the crow, \"but my beak is aching today. You fetch it, partner — I shall guard the grains.\" So the sparrow flew to the well and back, jug by tiny jug, while the crow guarded the grains, mostly from a comfortable branch, with his eyes shut.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"“लकड़ियां कौन इकट्ठी करेगा?” “मैं तो कर देता,” कौवा बोला, “लेकिन मेरा पंख अकड़ा हुआ है — कल तक बिल्कुल ठीक हो जाएगा। तुम ही इकट्ठी कर लो, साथी।” चिड़िया ने लकड़ियां इकट्ठी कर लीं। “हांड़ी कौन चलाएगा?” “मैं चला देता, लेकिन धुएं से मेरी आंखों में तकलीफ़ होती है। तुम चलाती रहो, साथी। तुम बहुत बढ़िया कर रही हो।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Who will gather the sticks?\" \"I would,\" said the crow, \"but my wing is stiff — tomorrow it will be perfect. You gather, partner.\" The sparrow gathered. \"Who will stir the pot?\" \"I would, but the smoke troubles my eyes. Stir on, partner. You are doing splendidly.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"और फिर सुनहरी और भाप छोड़ती खिचड़ी पककर तैयार हो गई, और तभी एक गज़ब का डॉक्टरी चमत्कार हुआ: कौवे की चोंच, पंख और आँखें—सब एक ही पल में बिल्कुल ठीक हो गए। \"साझीदार!\" अपनी थाली लेकर नीचे फुदकते हुए वह चिल्लाया, \"हमने कर दिखाया! निकालो हमारी खिचड़ी!\"","lang":"hi","body":"And then the khichdi was done, golden and steaming, and a remarkable medical miracle occurred: the crow's beak, wing and eyes all recovered in the same instant. \"Partner!\" he cried, hopping down with his plate. \"We have done it! Serve out our khichdi!\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"गौरैया ने कौवे की तरफ़ देखा। उसने उस हाँडी को देखा जिसे उसने भरा था, उस आग को देखा जिसे उसने सुलगाया था, और जिसे उसने अपने नन्हे हाथों के पूरे ज़ोर से चलाया था। हमारी खिचड़ी।","lang":"hi","body":"The sparrow looked at the crow. She looked at the pot she had filled, over the fire she had built, stirred with the strength of her small arms. Our khichdi.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chiri-kaan-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chiri-kaan:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sparrow, the Crow and the Khichdi","text":"और यहाँ याद रखने वाली बात यह है: अगली बार जब उन दोनों को दाने मिले, तो गौरैया के कहने से पहले ही कौवा पानी ले आया। दर्द करती चोंच के बावजूद। कुछ लोग तो कहते हैं कि उसने खिचड़ी चलाई भी। और सब मानते हैं कि वह खिचड़ी खाने में दोगुनी स्वादिष्ट लगी।","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the part worth keeping: the next time the two of them found grains, the crow fetched the water before the sparrow had finished asking. Aching beak and all. Some say he even stirred. The khichdi, everyone agrees, tasted twice as good.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chiri-kaan.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chiri-kaan|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"बहुत पुरानी बात है, पुराने पंजाब के सियालकोट में राजा सालवाहन के घर एक बेटा हुआ—और ज्योतिषियों ने सितारे देखकर एक अजीब हिदायत दी: बारह साल तक यह बालक बाहर किसी को दिखाई नहीं देना चाहिए। सो रसालू चारदीवारी के पीछे पला-बढ़ा, एक ऐसे महल में जहाँ दुनिया को छोड़कर बाकी सब कुछ था।","lang":"hi","body":"Long ago in Sialkot, in old Punjab, a son was born to King Salvahan — and the wise men read the stars and gave a strange instruction: for twelve years, the boy must not be seen abroad. So Rasalu grew up behind walls, in a palace with everything in it except the world.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"वह अकेला बड़ा नहीं हुआ। उसके दो ऐसे दोस्त थे जिन्हें लोकगीत कभी नहीं छोड़ते: एक अकलमंद तोता जो ज़्यादातर मंत्रियों से भी समझदारी की बात करता था, और भौंर इराक़ी नाम का एक बछेड़ा—कुछ गाने वाले कसम खाकर कहते हैं कि वह ठीक उसी रात पैदा हुआ था जिस रात रसालू का जन्म हुआ था, और वह उत्तर की किसी भी कहानी का सबसे तेज़ घोड़ा था।","lang":"hi","body":"He did not grow up alone. He had two friends the ballads never leave out: a wise parrot who talked better sense than most ministers, and a colt called Bhaunr Iraqi — foaled, some singers swear, on the very night Rasalu was born, and the fastest horse in any story of the north.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"दीवारों के पीछे से रसालू को बाहर की दुनिया सुनाई देती थी — घंटियों की आवाज़, पहियों की घड़घड़ाहट, शादियाँ, और दूसरों के खेतों पर बरसती बारिश। ग्यारह साल तक सिर्फ़ सुनते रहना बहुत लंबा वक़्त होता है। एक दिन, जब बारहवाँ साल शुरू ही हुआ था, वह दरवाज़े पर खड़ा था और सिटकनी पर उसका हाथ था।","lang":"hi","body":"From the walls, Rasalu could hear the world — bells, wheels, weddings, rain on other people's fields. Eleven years of listening is a long time. One day, with the twelfth year barely begun, he stood at the gate with his hand on the bolt.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"वह पंजाब की दुनिया में निकल पड़ा — नदियाँ, जंगल, चारदीवारी वाले शहर, अजनबियों से भरी सड़कें — और उसने देखा कि यह दुनिया ग्यारह साल तक सुनी बातों से कहीं बड़ी, अनोखी और बेहतर थी। और तुरंत ही लोकगीत हमें दिखाते हैं कि वह किस तरह का नायक बनने वाला था।","lang":"hi","body":"Out he went into Punjab — rivers, forests, walled towns, roads full of strangers — and found it bigger and stranger and better than eleven years of listening had promised. And straightaway the ballads show us what kind of hero he would be.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"गाने वाले कहते हैं कि रास्ते में रसालू हमेशा छोटी-छोटी बातों के लिए रुक जाया करता था। किसी फँसे हुए परिंदे को आज़ाद कर दिया। किसी मुसीबत में पड़े जीव की मदद कर दी, जबकि तोता देरी होने पर बड़बड़ाता रहता। लगभग हर लोकगीत में कोई न कोई पूछता है, \"इतनी झंझट की क्या ज़रूरत है?\" और रसालू जवाब देता है: आगे के रास्ते में की गई कोई भी भलाई कभी बेकार नहीं जाती।","lang":"hi","body":"For on the road, the singers say, Rasalu was forever stopping for small things. A trapped bird set loose. A creature in trouble helped out of it, while the parrot muttered about delays. \"Why bother?\" asks someone in nearly every ballad. And Rasalu answers: no kindness is wasted on the road ahead.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"और लोकगीत भी उसके इस नियम को पूरी तरह निभाते हैं: वे छोटे-छोटे जीव जिनकी उसने मदद की थी, ठीक सही वक़्त पर बार-बार लौटकर आते हैं — वक़्त पर दी गई चेतावनी, नाकाम की गई चाल, बचाई गई बाज़ी — हर नेकी कहानी में ठीक उसी पल लौट आती है जब नायक को उसकी सबसे ज़्यादा ज़रूरत होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the ballads keep his rule scrupulously: the small ones he helped come back, again and again, at exactly the right moment — a warning cried in time, a trick spoiled, a game saved — each good turn walking back into the story just when the hero needs it most.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.raja-rasalu-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.raja-rasalu:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Prince Who Rode Out of the Story","text":"उसके कारनामों से अनगिनत सर्दियों की रातें भर जाती हैं — चालाक राजाओं के साथ मुक़ाबले, पहेलियाँ, बाल-बाल बचना, और भौंर इराक़ी का चार पैरों वाले हर जानवर से आगे निकल जाना — और सदियों तक भाट गाँव-गाँव इन्हें गाते रहे, और हर किसी ने इसमें एक नई चमक जोड़ी।","lang":"hi","body":"His adventures fill winter nights beyond counting — contests with tricky kings, riddles, narrow escapes, Bhaunr Iraqi outrunning everything on four legs — and they were sung from village to village by bards for centuries, each one adding a polish.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-raja-rasalu.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.raja-rasalu|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Fields of Punjab and Haryana"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"उत्तराखंड के ऊँचे पहाड़ों में, जितना तुम सोच सकते हो उससे भी पास, दो नदियाँ जन्म लेती हैं। गंगोत्री के ऊपर की बर्फ़ से गंगा निकलती है। यमुनोत्री के ऊपर, बंदरपूँछ की ढलानों से यमुना निकलती है। पहाड़ों का एक ही पड़ोस; दो शुरुआतें।","lang":"hi","body":"High in the mountains of Uttarakhand, closer together than you might think, two rivers are born. From the ice above Gangotri comes the Ganga. From the flanks of Bandarpunch, above Yamunotri, comes the Yamuna. One mountain neighbourhood; two beginnings.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"इन पहाड़ों की परंपराओं में वे सिर्फ नदियाँ नहीं हैं। वे देवियाँ हैं, और—जैसा कि पुरानी कहानियों में सुनाया जाता है—वे दो बहनों जैसी हैं: एक ही ऊँचे देश में एक-दूसरे के पास जन्मीं, एक जैसी ही बर्फ के बीच पली-बढ़ीं, और एक-दूसरे से उतनी ही अलग जितनी दो बहनें हमेशा होती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"To the traditions of these hills they are not just rivers. They are goddesses, and — in the way the old stories are often told — they are like two sisters: born near each other in the same high country, raised among the same snows, and as different as two sisters always are.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"गंगा गरजती-शोर मचाती हुई नीचे उतरती हैं। वे बड़ी हैं, मशहूर हैं—ऋषिकेश से उछलती-कूदती, हरिद्वार में पहाड़ों से बाहर कदम रखती हुई, दूसरी नदियों को सहेलियों की तरह साथ समेटती हुई, जहाँ मैदानों के बड़े-बड़े शहर अपने किनारों को सजाकर उनके आने पर घंटियाँ बजाने का इंतज़ार करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Ganga comes down loud. She is the elder, the famous one — leaping through Rishikesh, striding out of the hills at Haridwar, gathering tributaries like companions, with the great cities of the plains waiting to line her banks and ring bells at her arrival.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"यमुना कुछ साँवली और शांत होकर नीचे उतरती हैं, अपनी ही धुन में। जहाँ गंगा का पानी चमकीला बहता है, वहीं यमुना का पानी गहरा नीला-हरा होकर बहता है। उनका रास्ता दूर तक घूमकर निकलता है, जंगलों और पुरानी रियासतों के पास से—और आगे चलकर, सीधे दिल्ली के तख़्त और खुद ताज महल के पास से।","lang":"hi","body":"Yamuna comes down darker and quieter, keeping her own counsel. Her waters run a deep blue-green where Ganga's run bright. Her road swings wide and away, past forests and old kingdoms — and, in her middle years, right past the throne of Delhi and the Taj Mahal itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"सैकड़ों-सैकड़ों किलोमीटर तक दोनों के रास्ते अलग-अलग रहते हैं—इतनी दूर कि एक नदी के किनारे बैठा बच्चा शायद कभी दूसरी के बारे में सोचे भी न। लेकिन पहाड़ों की कहानियाँ इस बात पर मुस्कुरा देती हैं, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे दूरियों के झगड़ों पर दादियाँ मुस्कुरा देती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"For hundreds and hundreds of kilometres the two roads stay apart — so far apart that a child by one river might never think of the other. But the hill tellings smile at that, the way grandmothers smile at quarrels about distance.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"और अचरज की बात यह है: आप इसे खुद देख सकते हैं। संगम पर नावें आपको ठीक उसी जगह ले जाती हैं जहाँ दोनों नदियाँ मिलती हैं—और वे सचमुच दो अलग रंगों की दिखती हैं, एक हल्की और दूसरी गहरी, एक ही बहाव में साथ-साथ बहती हुई, जैसे दो बहनें बाहों में बाहें डाले चल रही हों और फिर भी अपनी-अपनी पहचान बनाए हुए हों।","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the wonder: you can see it. At the Sangam, boats take you to the exact place where the two waters meet — and they truly are two colours, the pale and the deep running side by side in one bed, like two sisters walking arm in arm, still recognisably themselves.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"यह भारत के सबसे पवित्र मिलन-स्थलों में से एक है, जहाँ त्योहारों के बरसों में भारी मेले जुड़ते हैं। परंपरा इस मिलन में एक तीसरी बहन को भी जोड़ती है—सरस्वती, जो अनदेखी हैं, कहानियों में मौजूद भले ही कोई आँख उन्हें ढूँढ न पाए। पहाड़ों की मान्यता है: परिवार के कुछ सदस्य बिना दिखे भी साथ आते हैं। उनकी भी गिनती होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"It is one of the most sacred meeting-places in India, where vast gatherings assemble in festival years. Tradition adds a third sister to the meeting — the Saraswati, the unseen one, present in story though no eye finds her. The hills say: some family members attend invisibly. They still count.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Two Sisters Who Took Different Roads","text":"\"वहाँ ऊपर उत्तराखंड में, तीर्थयात्री आज भी दोनों उद्गमों की चढ़ाई चढ़ते हैं — गंगोत्री और यमुनोत्री, जो पहाड़ों के चार पवित्र धामों में से दो हैं — ताकि हर बहन से उसके अपने ऊँचे घर में मिल सकें, जहाँ वे बस एक चमकती, ठंडी धारा भर हैं जिसे कोई बच्चा भी एक कदम में लाँघ ले।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Back up in Uttarakhand, pilgrims still climb to both beginnings — Gangotri and Yamunotri, two of the four holy places of the hills — to greet each sister in her own high home, where each is only a bright cold stream a child could step across.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ganga-yamuna-sisters.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ganga-yamuna-sisters|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"\"जिम कॉर्बेट का जन्म करीब डेढ़ सौ साल पहले नैनीताल में हुआ था, जो आज के उत्तराखंड की कुमाऊँ पहाड़ियों में है। वे खुद भी लगभग आधे-जंगली जैसे ही बड़े हुए — एक ऐसे लड़के की तरह जिसने अपना हर मुमकिन पल जंगल में बिताया, जब तक कि वह उसे किसी किताब की तरह पढ़ना और उसकी ख़तरे की पुकारों व सन्नाटों की भाषा बोलना न सीख गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Jim Corbett was born about a hundred and fifty years ago in Nainital, in the Kumaon hills of what is now Uttarakhand, and grew up half-wild himself — a boy who spent every possible hour in the forest, until he could read it like a book and speak its language of alarm calls and silences.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"\"इसी हुनर ने उन्हें वक़्त के साथ वह इंसान बना दिया, जिन्हें पहाड़ी गाँव वाले अपनी सबसे बड़ी मुसीबत में बुलावा भेजते थे। बहुत ही कम ऐसा होता था कि कोई बाघ या तेंदुआ — जो आमतौर पर बूढ़ा, ज़ख्मी, या अपने जंगली शिकार से महरूम हो — इंसानों का शिकार करने लगे, और पूरी की पूरी घाटियाँ ख़ौफ़ के साए में जीने लगें। तब कॉर्बेट अकेले और पैदल आते, और इस ख़तरे को ख़त्म कर देते।\"","lang":"hi","body":"That skill made him, in time, the man the hill villages sent for in their worst trouble. Very rarely, a tiger or leopard — usually old, hurt, or robbed of its wild prey — turned to hunting people, and whole valleys lived in terror. Corbett would come, alone and on foot, and end the danger.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"\"उन्होंने सालों तक अपनी जान जोखिम में डालकर यह किया, गाँव वालों से कभी कोई पैसा नहीं लिया, और पहाड़ के लोग उन पर आँख मूँदकर भरोसा करने लगे। लेकिन उन लंबी, ख़ामोश पगडंडियों पर कुछ और भी हो रहा था: पूरे भारत में कोई भी जंगली बाघों को इतने करीब से नहीं देख रहा था, जितना वह इंसान जिसे उनमें से चंद का शिकार करने भेजा गया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He did this for years, at great risk, refusing payment from the villagers, and the hill people came to trust him completely. But something else was happening on all those long quiet walks: nobody in India was watching wild tigers more closely than the man sent to hunt a few of them.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"\"और साल-दर-साल जो कुछ उन्होंने देखा, उसने उन्हें और भी ज़्यादा बेचैन कर दिया। जंगल सिमटते जा रहे थे। बंदूकें हर तरफ़ थीं, और बाघ का शिकार करना एक फ़ैशनेबल खेल बन चुका था। वह जानवर जिसे वे — खुद उनके लिखे शब्दों में — 'एक बड़े दिल वाला शरीफ़ इंसान' मानते थे, इससे पहले कि भारत कुछ समझ पाता, भारत से गायब होता जा रहा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And what he saw, year after year, troubled him more and more. The forests were shrinking. Guns were everywhere, and shooting a tiger had become a fashionable sport. The animal he considered — his own written words — a large-hearted gentleman was disappearing from India before India had noticed.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"तो देश के सबसे मशहूर शिकारी के सामने एक अजीब सवाल आ खड़ा हुआ: जिस दुनिया में बाघ ख़त्म होते जा रहे हों, वहाँ कोई अपने हुनर का क्या करे?","lang":"hi","body":"So the most famous hunter in the country faced a strange question: what should a man do with skills like his, in a world running out of tigers?","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"उन्होंने उस ज़माने में जंगली बाघों की फ़िल्में बनाईं और तस्वीरें खींचीं, जब दुनिया में शायद ही किसी ने ऐसा किया था। उन्होंने स्कूली बच्चों को जाकर बताया कि जंगल क्यों इतने ज़रूरी हैं। उन्होंने किताबें लिखीं — 'मैन-ईटर्स ऑफ़ कुमाऊँ' ने तो उन्हें पूरी दुनिया में मशहूर कर दिया — और अपने कारनामों के बीच-बीच में, उन्होंने जंगल के लिए प्यार और उसके भविष्य की चिंता उन पन्नों में भर दी।","lang":"hi","body":"He filmed and photographed wild tigers when almost no one on Earth had done it. He gave talks to schoolchildren about why the forest mattered. He wrote books — Man-Eaters of Kumaon made him famous across the world — and filled them, between adventures, with love for the jungle and alarm for its future.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"और उन्होंने बाकी लोगों के साथ मिलकर उस चीज़ के लिए ज़ोर लगाया जो उस वक़्त भारत में न के बराबर थी: सुरक्षित ज़मीन, जहाँ जंगल और उसके जानवरों को बिना छेड़े छोड़ दिया जाए। उनकी प्यारी कुमाऊँ की तलहटी का एक विशाल रिज़र्व भारत के पहले राष्ट्रीय उद्यानों में से एक बना — और उनके गुज़रने के बाद उनके सम्मान में उसका नाम बदलकर 'कॉर्बेट नेशनल पार्क' रख दिया गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And he pushed, with others, for something India barely had then: protected land, where the forest and its animals would simply be left alone. A great reserve in his beloved Kumaon foothills became one of India's first national parks — and after his death it was renamed in his honour: Corbett National Park.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.corbett-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.corbett:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Hunter Who Put Down His Rifle","text":"दशकों बाद, जब भारत ने बाघों को विलुप्त होने से बचाने के लिए अपनी सबसे बड़ी मुहिम शुरू की, तो उसकी शुरुआत इसी पार्क से हुई। आख़िरकार, उस शिकारी का बदला हुआ दिल पूरे देश की नीति बन चुका था।","lang":"hi","body":"Decades later, when India launched its great campaign to save the tiger from extinction, that park was where it began. The hunter's changed heart had become, in the end, national policy.","art":"art/story/sm/it-corbett.jpg","route":"#/story/it.corbett|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"उत्तराखंड की किसी भी बड़ी पहाड़ी पर चढ़ो तो जंगल भी तुम्हारे साथ-साथ ऊपर चढ़ता है — पहले बाँज, फिर बुरांश, फिर देवदार और चीड़ — जब तक कि अचानक से पेड़ ख़त्म न हो जाएँ। उस रेखा के ऊपर पहाड़ खुली घास की चादर ओढ़ लेता है: बादलों को छूते, दूर तक फैले मखमली घास के मैदान, जिन्हें बुग्याल कहते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Climb any big hill in Uttarakhand and the forest climbs with you — oak, then rhododendron, then deodar and fir — until, quite suddenly, the trees stop. Above that line the mountain wears open grass: rolling, cloud-brushed meadows called bugyals.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"गर्मियों में बुग्याल फूलों से झूम उठते हैं — नीले पॉपी, पोटेंटिला, और बर्फ़ीली चोटियों के साए में रंगों से भरी पूरी की पूरी ढलानें — और गढ़वाल तथा कुमाऊँ के गड़ेरिये अपने रेवड़ों को चराने ऊपर ले जाते हैं, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे उनके परिवार तब से करते आ रहे हैं जितने पुराने लोगों के गीत हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"In summer the bugyals go mad with flowers — blue poppies, potentillas, whole slopes of colour with snow peaks standing over them — and the shepherds of Garhwal and Kumaon walk their flocks up to graze, as their families have for as long as anyone's songs remember.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"लेकिन पहाड़ का हर बच्चा बचपन में ही सीख जाता है: बुग्याल कोई आम चरागाह नहीं होते। इन ऊँचे घास के मैदानों को देवताओं — यानी पहाड़ों के भगवानों के बगीचे और रहने की जगह माना जाता है। वहाँ आप एक मेहमान हैं। और मेहमानों का एक सलीका होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"But every hill child learns early: a bugyal is not an ordinary pasture. These high meadows are held to be the gardens and dwelling-grounds of the devtas — the gods of the hills. You are a guest up there. And guests have manners.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"पुराने नियम बड़े पक्के हैं, और गड़ेरिये आज भी उनका पालन करते हैं। धीरे-धीरे चलो और चिल्लाओ मत — ये ऊँचाइयाँ शोर मचाने की जगह नहीं हैं। अपने जानवरों के चरने के अलावा वहाँ से कुछ मत लो। किसी भी तरह की गंदगी मत छोड़ो। कुछ मैदानों को तो बिल्कुल भी नहीं छेड़ना है, और आदर के कारण उनके ऊपर की कुछ चोटियों पर कभी नहीं चढ़ना है।","lang":"hi","body":"The old rules are quite exact, and shepherds keep them still. Walk gently and do not shout — the heights are not a place for noise. Take nothing but what your animals graze. Leave no mess of any kind. Certain meadows are not to be disturbed at all, and some peaks above them are never to be climbed, out of respect.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"अपने दादाजी के रेवड़ के साथ पहली बार जा रहे एक लड़के ने एक बार वही सीधा सा सवाल पूछा: क्या देवताओं को सचमुच शोर और गंदगी से बुरा लगता है?","lang":"hi","body":"A boy going up for his first season with his grandfather's flock once asked the obvious question: do the gods really mind noise and mess?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"और यह सच भी है: ये नियम चाहे जो भी हों, असल में प्रकृति की रक्षा ही हैं। वे मैदान जहाँ कोई चिल्लाता नहीं, खुदाई नहीं करता, कचरा नहीं फैलाता या हद से ज़्यादा समय नहीं रुकता, वही मैदान हैं जहाँ घास पहाड़ की नाज़ुक मिट्टी को बाँधे रखती है, झरने साफ़ बहते हैं, और फूल हर एक गर्मी में फिर से खिल उठते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And it is true: the rules are conservation, whatever else they are. Meadows where no one shouts, digs, litters or overstays are meadows where the grass holds the thin mountain soil, the streams run clean, and the flowers return every single summer.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bugyal-rules-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bugyal-rules:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Meadows Above the Trees","text":"बुग्यालों पर अब नए खतरे हैं — मशहूर जगहों पर बहुत ज़्यादा सैलानी, और सभी जगहों पर बदलता मौसम — इसलिए अदालतों और गाँवों दोनों ने मिलकर उनकी रक्षा के लिए कदम उठाए हैं, और ऐसे नियम बनाए हैं जो बिल्कुल दादाजी के नियमों जैसे ही लगते हैं: धीरे से जाओ, कुछ भी मत लाओ, कुछ भी मत छोड़ो।","lang":"hi","body":"The bugyals face new pressures now — too many visitors in famous ones, changing weather in all of them — and courts and villages have both stepped in to protect them, with rules that sound remarkably like the grandfather's: go gently, take nothing, leave nothing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bugyal-rules.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bugyal-rules|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"गढ़वाल और कुमाऊँ के ऊपर नंदा देवी खड़ी हैं — भारत के सबसे ऊँचे पर्वतों में से एक, और सिर्फ़ एक पर्वत से कहीं बढ़कर। पहाड़ के लोगों के लिए वह नंदा हैं, यानी देवी — और बड़े लाड़-प्यार से, वह इन पहाड़ों की अपनी बेटी भी हैं, जिनका ब्याह ऊँचे बर्फीले पहाड़ों में हुआ है।","lang":"hi","body":"Over Garhwal and Kumaon stands Nanda Devi — one of the highest mountains in India, and much more than a mountain. To the hill people she is Nanda, the goddess — and, tenderly, she is also the hills' own daughter, married into the high snows.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"क्योंकि पहाड़ों की कहानियों में, नंदा इसी धरती की बेटी हैं, जिनका ब्याह भगवान शिव से हुआ है, जिनका वास गहरे हिमालय में है। और दूर ब्याही गई हर पहाड़ी बेटी की तरह, वह भी अपने मायके — अपनी माँ के घर — मिलने आती हैं, और फिर समय आने पर, उन्हें पैदल विदा करके वापस ससुराल पहुँचाना होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"For in the hills' telling, Nanda is a daughter of this very country, wedded to Lord Shiva, whose home is the deep Himalaya. And like every pahari daughter married far away, she comes back to visit her maika — her mother's home — and must, in time, be walked back to her husband's.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"हर साल उनके लिए छोटे-छोटे त्योहार होते हैं। लेकिन लगभग हर बारह साल में एक बार आता है महा-उत्सव — नंदा देवी राज जात — जब पूरा पहाड़ी इलाका अपनी बेटी को पूरे ठाठ-बाट से विदा करने के लिए इकट्ठा होता है। लोग इसके लिए अपना पूरा बचपन इंतज़ार करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Every year there are small festivals for her. But roughly once every twelve years comes the great one — the Nanda Devi Raj Jat — when the whole country of the hills assembles to escort its daughter home in state. People wait their whole childhoods for it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"यह यात्रा पैदल चलती है। कोई कहावत नहीं: सचमुच पैदल चलती है, लगभग तीन हफ़्तों तक, गढ़वाल के गाँव-गाँव से होते हुए ऊपर — पालकी में बैठी देवी, भीड़ के ऊपर डोलती घाटी के मंदिरों की सुनहरी छतरियाँ, और पुराने रिवाज़ के मुताबिक सबसे आगे, एक चौसिंग्या खाडू: चार सींगों वाला मेढ़ा, जो इसी यात्रा के लिए जन्मा है और आगे-आगे रास्ता दिखाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The procession walks. Not a metaphor: it walks, for about three weeks, village to village up through Garhwal — the goddess in her palanquin, gold umbrellas from valley temples bobbing over the crowds, and at the head of everything, by old custom, a chausingya khadu: a four-horned ram, born for the journey, who leads the way.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"हर पड़ाव अपने घर लौटने जैसा है। रास्ते के गाँव देवी को रात भर के लिए अपने परिवार की तरह ठहराते हैं — गीत, दीये, आँसू, त्योहार का खाना — क्योंकि वह सिर्फ़ उनके गाँव से गुज़र नहीं रही हैं। वह उनकी अपनी हैं, जो लंबी बर्फ़ में जाने से पहले, एक आख़िरी रात के लिए मिलने आई हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Every halt is a homecoming. Villages on the route host the goddess overnight as family — songs, lamps, tears, festival food — because she is not passing through their village. She is theirs, visiting, one last night before the long snows.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"और रास्ते भर गाए जाने वाले गीत एक खास तरह के होते हैं, जिन्हें हर पहाड़ी परिवार अपनी रग-रग से जानता है: विदाई के गीत। विदाई के गीत — यानी वो गीत जो तब गाए जाते हैं जब कोई बेटी अपने मायके से विदा होकर ससुराल जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the songs along the road are a particular kind that every hill family knows in its bones: vidaai songs. Farewell songs — the songs sung when a daughter leaves her parents' home for her husband's.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"सफ़र के आख़िरी पड़ाव गाँवों से आगे, बुग्यालों के पार, वीरान ऊँचाइयों से होते हुए पहाड़ की तरफ़ बढ़ते हैं — जहाँ आख़िरकार विदाई होती है, और वह मेढ़ा सारे पहाड़ों का प्यार समेटे आख़िरी सफ़र पर अकेले ही बर्फ़ की ओर आगे बढ़ जाता है, और लोग अपने घरों की तरफ़ लौट पड़ते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The last marches climb beyond the villages, beyond the bugyals, into the bare high country toward the mountain — where at last the farewell is made, and the ram goes on ahead alone toward the snows, carrying the hills' love the final distance, and the people turn for home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.nanda-raj-jat-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.nanda-raj-jat:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Walking the Goddess Home","text":"वे नीचे उतरते हैं तो मन एक साथ हल्का भी होता है और भारी भी, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे किसी सच्ची विदाई के बाद होता है। और कहते हैं कि उस रात गाँवों में अगली राज जात की बातें होने लगती हैं — जो बारह साल बाद आनी है — और यह कि अगली बार कौन-से बच्चे इतने बड़े हो जाएँगे जो पूरा रास्ता पैदल चल सकें।","lang":"hi","body":"They walk back down lighter and heavier at once, the way you are after a true goodbye. And in villages that night, they say, the talk is of the next Raj Jat — twelve years off — and which children will be old enough to walk the whole way, next time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-nanda-raj-jat.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.nanda-raj-jat|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Stories from the High Hills"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"यह एक ऐसी कहानी है जो बंगाली दादियाँ-नानियाँ बहुत पुराने समय से सोते वक़्त सुनाती आई हैं। शहर के बाहर एक गाँव में, एक बूढ़े कुम्हार को नदी में लकड़ी के बक्से में बहते हुए तीन बच्चे मिले। वह उन्हें घर ले आया, उनके नाम अरुण, बरुण और किरणमाला रखे, और उन्हें अपने बच्चों की तरह पाला।","lang":"hi","body":"This is a story Bengali grandmothers have been telling at bedtime for a very long time. In a village outside the city, an old potter once found three babies floating down the river in a wooden box. He brought them home and named them Arun, Barun and Kiranmala, and raised them as his own.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"वे बड़े हो गए। और एक शाम एक मुसाफ़िर उनके दरवाज़े पर रुका, उनका पानी पिया, और उन्हें उस पहाड़ के बारे में बताया — जो उत्तर की सड़क के छोर पर है, जहाँ तीन नामुमकिन चीज़ें रखी हैं: एक बोलने वाली चिड़िया, एक गाने वाला पेड़, और ऐसा पानी जो सोए हुओं को जगा देता है।","lang":"hi","body":"They grew up. And one evening a traveller stopped at their door, drank their water, and told them about the mountain — the one at the end of the north road, where three impossible things are kept: a bird that talks, a tree that sings, and water that wakes the sleeping.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"\"तो फिर मैं जाकर उन्हें लेकर आऊँगा,\" सबसे बड़े भाई, अरुण ने कहा। मुसाफ़िर ने अपना प्याला नीचे रखा। \"हर कोई यही कहता है। सुनो। ऊपर के रास्ते पर, पीछे से आवाज़ें तुम्हारा नाम पुकारती हैं — तुम्हारी माँ, तुम्हारा भाई, तुम्हारा अपना कुत्ता। एक बार भी पीछे मुड़े, तो तुम पहाड़ी की ढलान पर एक पत्थर बन जाओगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Then I shall go and get them,\" said Arun, the eldest. The traveller put down his cup. \"Everyone says that. Listen. On the path up, voices call your name from behind you — your mother, your brother, your own dog. Turn round even once and you become a stone on the hillside.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"अरुण गया। आधे रास्ते पर, पीछे से किसी ने रोते-बिलखते हुए, उसकी छोटी बहन की आवाज़ में उसका नाम पुकारा। वह मुड़ा। वह घर नहीं लौटा। फिर बरुण गया, अपने कानों में कपड़ा ठूँसकर — पर कपड़ा गिर पड़ा, और वह भी मुड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Arun went. Halfway up, somebody behind him called his name in his little sister's voice, sobbing. He turned. He did not come home. Barun went next, with his ears stopped up with cloth — and the cloth fell out, and he turned too.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"\"मुझे मशक दे दीजिए,\" किरणमाला ने बूढ़े कुम्हार से कहा। उन्होंने उसे कसकर पकड़े रखा। \"अब मेरे पास बस तुम ही बची हो।\" \"तो फिर जब मैं वापस आऊँ तब मुझे थाम लीजिएगा,\" उसने कहा, \"जब वे तीनों मेरे पीछे होंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Give me the water skin,\" said Kiranmala to the old potter. He held on to it. \"You are the last one I have.\" \"Then hold on to me when I get back,\" she said, \"with all three of them behind me.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"रास्ता सफ़ेद पत्थरों वाला और बहुत खड़ी चढ़ाई का था, और उस पर ऐसे भारी पत्थर बिखरे थे जो हूबहू नौजवानों के आकार और कद के थे। और फिर आवाज़ें शुरू हुईं। अरुण की आवाज़। बरुण की आवाज़। उसका नाम पुकारती हुईं, इतनी पास से कि मानो छू ही लें।","lang":"hi","body":"The path was white stone and very steep, and it was covered in boulders that were exactly the size and shape of young men. And then the voices started. Arun's voice. Barun's voice. Calling her name, close enough to touch.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"सबसे ऊपर, सोने के एक पिंजरे में बोलने वाली चिड़िया बैठी थी। उसने उसे ऊपर से नीचे तक देखा। \"सौ साल हो गए,\" उसने कहा, \"और तुम पहली हो जो पीछे नहीं मुड़ी। गाने वाली डाली ले लो। पानी ले लो। और जल्दी करो — पहाड़ी इंतज़ार कर रही है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At the top, in a cage of gold, sat the bird that talks. It looked her up and down. \"A hundred years,\" it said, \"and you are the first one who did not turn round. Take the singing branch. Take the water. And be quick — the hillside is waiting.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.kiranmala-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.kiranmala:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Kiranmala and the Mountain of Voices","text":"वह रास्ते की चट्टानों पर पानी छिड़कती हुई नीचे उतरने लगी, और उसके पीछे-पीछे पूरी पहाड़ी उठ खड़ी हुई: नौजवान और बूढ़े, एक चरवाहा, एक व्यापारी, और दो ऐसे भाई जो इतने लंबे समय से पत्थर बने हुए थे कि बोलना ही भूल चुके थे। सब एक साथ घर की ओर चल पड़े, और पूरा गाँव बाहर निकल आया।","lang":"hi","body":"She went down sprinkling water on the boulders as she passed, and the hillside stood up behind her: young men and old men, a shepherd, a merchant, and two brothers who had been stone so long they had forgotten how to talk. They walked home in a crowd, and the whole village came out.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-kiranmala.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.kiranmala|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"शहर में मिठाई की एक दुकान थी, जिसके दरवाज़े से इतनी बढ़िया ख़ुशबू आती थी कि वहाँ से गुज़रने वाले लोग अपने कदम धीमे कर लेते थे। एक ग़रीब आदमी बाहर सीढ़ी पर बैठकर अपनी सूखी रोटी खाया करता था, क्योंकि उस दरवाज़े पर बैठकर सूखी रोटी खाने से भी गरमा-गरम जलेबी जैसा स्वाद आता था।","lang":"hi","body":"There was a sweet-shop in the town with a doorway that smelled so good that people slowed down as they passed it. A poor man used to eat his dry roti sitting on the step outside, because dry roti eaten in that doorway tasted of hot jalebi.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"एक दिन दुकानदार अपना बही-खाता लेकर बाहर आया। \"छह महीने से तुम यहाँ बैठे हो। छह महीने से मेरी ख़ुशबू ले रहे हो। तुम्हें मुझे आठ रुपये देने होंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One day the shopkeeper came out with his account book. \"Six months you have been sitting there. Six months of my smell. You owe me eight rupees.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"उस ग़रीब आदमी के पास आठ रुपये वैसे ही थे जैसे किसी मछली के पास जेबें होती हैं। बहस इतनी बढ़ गई कि दोनों को पकड़कर राजा कृष्णचंद्र के दरबार में ले जाया गया — जिन्होंने दोनों को देखा, एक ठंडी साँस भरी, और गोपाल भार को बुलवाया।","lang":"hi","body":"The poor man had eight rupees the way a fish has pockets. The argument got loud enough that they were both marched off to the court of Raja Krishnachandra — who looked at both of them, sighed, and sent for Gopal Bhar.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"\"ज़रा मैं भी अच्छी तरह समझ लूँ,\" गोपाल ने कहा। \"इसने आपकी कोई चीज़ नहीं खाई।\" \"कुछ नहीं।\" \"इसने आपकी किसी चीज़ को हाथ नहीं लगाया।\" \"कुछ नहीं।\" \"मगर इसने सूँघा।\" \"पूरे छह महीने तक!\" दुकानदार ने कहा। \"तब तो यह बड़ा आसान है,\" गोपाल ने कहा, और सिक्कों की एक थैली मँगवाई।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Let me be sure I understand,\" said Gopal. \"He ate nothing of yours.\" \"Nothing.\" \"He touched nothing of yours.\" \"Nothing.\" \"But he smelled.\" \"For six months!\" said the shopkeeper. \"Then this is easy,\" said Gopal, and asked for a bag of coins.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"पूरा दरबार आगे झुक आया। गोपाल ने थैली उठाई और दुकानदार के कान के ठीक पास ले जाकर पकड़ी।","lang":"hi","body":"The whole court leaned in. Gopal took the bag and held it up beside the shopkeeper's ear.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"छन-छन-छन सिक्के खनखनाए। गोपाल रुका, और उसने थैली का मुँह बाँध दिया। \"हिसाब चुकता,\" उसने कहा। \"इसने आपकी मिठाइयों की ख़ुशबू ली। आपने इसके पैसों की खनक सुन ली। अब किसी का किसी पर कुछ बाकी नहीं रहा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Chhan-chhan-chhan went the coins. Gopal stopped, and tied the bag shut. \"Paid,\" he said. \"He had the smell of your sweets. You have had the sound of his money. Nobody is owed anything.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gopal-smell-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gopal-smell:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Paying for the Smell","text":"दुकानदार ने अपना मुँह खोला, समझा कि कहने को तो कुछ बचा ही नहीं, और उसे फिर बंद कर लिया। राजा इतनी ज़ोर से हँसे कि उन्हें पानी देना पड़ा।","lang":"hi","body":"The shopkeeper opened his mouth, worked out that there was nothing at all to say, and closed it again. The Raja laughed so hard he had to be handed water.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gopal-smell.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gopal-smell|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"तेनाली रामन राजा कृष्णदेवराय के दरबार के सबसे मज़ाकिया आदमी थे, जिसका मतलब था कि वे चुपके से सबसे चतुर भी थे। एक गर्म रात वे जागे हुए लेटे थे कि उन्हें बगीचे में कुछ सुनाई दिया जो हवा बिलकुल नहीं थी: चार आदमी, फुसफुसाते हुए, केले के पेड़ों के बीच से दबे पाँव जा रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Tenali Raman was the funniest man at the court of King Krishnadevaraya, which meant he was also, quietly, the cleverest. One hot night he was lying awake when he heard something in the garden that was not the wind: four men, whispering, going carefully through the plantains.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"उन्होंने उनकी आवाज़ों से गिना। चार। एक वे खुद थे, दूसरी उनकी पत्नी, और पहरेदार सड़क पर इतनी दूर थे कि आवाज़ भी न पहुँचे।","lang":"hi","body":"He counted them by their voices. Four. He was one, his wife was two, and the guards were a long shout away down the road.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"\"सुनती हो!\" रामन ऐसी फुसफुसाहट में बोले जो अगली गली तक सुनाई दे सकती थी। \"शहर में चोर आ गए हैं! जल्दी करो — हर सिक्का, हर ज़ंजीर, चाँदी की हर थाली — उनके आने से पहले सब कुएँ में डाल दो!\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"WIFE!\" said Raman, in a whisper you could have heard in the next street. \"There are thieves in the town! Quick — every coin, every chain, every silver plate — into the well with it, before they come!\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"उनकी पत्नी, जिनका विवाह उनसे हुए कई साल हो चुके थे और जो उनकी बातें तुरंत समझ जाती थीं, उतनी ही धीमी आवाज़ में बोलीं, \"हाँ जी!\" फिर वे दोनों एक के बाद एक बक्सा कुएँ तक ले गए और अंदर पलट दिया। छपाक। छपाक। छपाक।","lang":"hi","body":"His wife, who had been married to him for years and had learned to keep up, said \"YES, HUSBAND!\" just as quietly. Then the two of them carried box after box out to the well and tipped them in. Sploosh. Sploosh. Sploosh.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"केले के पेड़ों के पीछे, चार चोरों ने एक-दूसरे को देखा। \"एक-एक सिक्का,\" एक ने फुसफुसाते हुए कहा। \"कुएँ के अंदर,\" दूसरे ने धीरे से कहा। \"हमें बस बाल्टियाँ चाहिए,\" तीसरे ने बुदबुदाया। चौथे चोर को कुछ गड़बड़ लग रही थी, पर बाकी तीनों के आगे उसकी एक न चली।","lang":"hi","body":"Behind the plantains, four thieves looked at one another. \"Every coin,\" breathed one. \"In a well,\" breathed another. \"We only need buckets,\" breathed the third. The fourth one, who had a bad feeling, was outvoted.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"वे पूरी रात उस कुएँ को खाली करते रहे। बाल्टी पर बाल्टी, एक के बाद एक बाल्टी, और हर बाल्टी का पानी छलकते हुए रामन की सब्ज़ियों की क्यारियों में गिरता गया क्योंकि उसे डालने के लिए उनके पास कोई और जगह ही नहीं थी। सुबह होते-होते, जब वे कुएँ की तली तक पहुँचे, तो उन्हें मिले: पत्थर। ढेर सारे पत्थर।","lang":"hi","body":"They emptied that well all night. Bucket after bucket after bucket, and every bucket went sloshing out over Raman's vegetable beds because they had nowhere else to put it. At the bottom, at dawn, they found: stones. A great many stones.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-thieves-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-thieves:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Thieves Who Watered the Garden","text":"रामन ने खिड़की के पट खोले, अंगड़ाई ली, और बाहर खड़े उन चार थके-हारे आदमियों को देखा जो एक ऐसे बगीचे में खड़े थे जिसे पहले कभी इतने शानदार ढंग से पानी नहीं मिला था। \"कमाल का काम किया,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"अगले मंगलवार भी इसी समय?\"","lang":"hi","body":"Raman opened his shutters, stretched, and looked out at four exhausted men standing in a garden that had never been so beautifully watered. \"Marvellous work,\" he said. \"Same time next Tuesday?\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-thieves.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-thieves|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"दक्षिण के बिल्कुल आखिरी छोर पर, जहाँ ज़मीन खत्म होती है, राम की सेना समुद्र के पार लंका तक एक पुल बना रही थी। वानर घर जितने बड़े-बड़े पत्थर उठा रहे थे। उनमें से कुछ तो सचमुच के पहाड़ ही उठाए चले आ रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"At the very tip of the south, where the land runs out, Rama's army was building a bridge across the sea to Lanka. The vanaras were carrying boulders the size of houses. Some of them were carrying actual hills.","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"एक चट्टान पर बैठी एक छोटी धारीदार गिलहरी करीब चार मिनट तक उन्हें देखती रही। फिर वह दौड़कर पानी के पास गई, गीली रेत में तब तक लोट-पोट हुई जब तक कि वह पूरी तरह रेत से सन न गई, फिर दौड़कर पुल पर पहुँची और खुद को ज़ोर से झटक दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"A small striped squirrel watched them from a rock for about four minutes. Then she ran down to the water, rolled in the wet sand until she was completely coated in it, ran out onto the bridge, and shook herself.","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"एक वानर का पैर उस पर पड़ते-पड़ते बचा। \"रास्ते से हटो, नन्ही सी जान! हम यहाँ पहाड़ उठा रहे हैं और तुम यहाँ धूल झाड़ रही हो!\"","lang":"hi","body":"A vanara nearly stepped on her. \"Out of the way, little thing! We are carrying mountains here and you are shaking dust about!\"","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"\"तुम्हारे पहाड़ों के बीच की खाली जगहें मेरे शरीर जितनी बड़ी हैं,\" गिलहरी ने कहा, और और रेत लाने वापस चली गई। वह कोई बात साबित नहीं कर रही थी। वह तो काम कर रही थी।","lang":"hi","body":"\"The gaps between your mountains are the size of my body,\" said the squirrel, and went back for more sand. She was not making a point. She was working.","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"दोपहर होते-होते वानर उस पर हँसने लगे, और उनमें से एक ने उसे पूँछ से उठाया और घुमाकर पुल से दूर फेंक दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"By afternoon the monkeys had started laughing at her, and one of them picked her up by the tail and swung her away off the bridge.","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"वह सीधे एक हाथ में जा गिरी। राम ने उसे थाम लिया था। उन्होंने उसे अपनी हथेली पर बिठाया और पुल की तरफ देखा, जहाँ हर पत्थर के बीच की हर खाली जगह गीली रेत से कसकर भर दी गई थी। \"इसके बिना,\" उन्होंने कहा, \"यह पूरा ढाँचा हिल जाता। तुम्हें यह किसने बताया?\" \"किसी ने नहीं,\" गिलहरी बोली। \"मैंने तो बस देखा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"She landed in a hand. Rama had caught her. He set her on his palm and looked at the bridge, where every gap between every boulder had been packed tight with wet sand. \"Without this,\" he said, \"the whole thing shifts. Who told you?\" \"Nobody,\" said the squirrel. \"I just looked.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ep.squirrel-bridge-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ep.squirrel-bridge:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Squirrel Who Built the Bridge","text":"\"उसे नीचे रखने से पहले, उन्होंने तीन उँगलियों से उसकी पीठ सहलाई। और पूरे दक्षिण में लोग तुम्हें यही बताएंगे कि तुम्हारी दीवार पर दौड़ने वाली नन्ही गिलहरी की पीठ पर आज भी तीन हल्की धारियाँ क्यों हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He stroked her back with three fingers before he put her down. And that, they will tell you all over the south, is why the little palm squirrel who runs up your wall has three pale stripes down her back to this day.","art":"art/story/sm/ep-squirrel-bridge.jpg","route":"#/story/ep.squirrel-bridge|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More from the Epics"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"हर साल ओणम पर, पूरे केरल के घरों में पूकलम सजाया जाता है — मुख्य दरवाज़े के पास ज़मीन पर फूलों की पंखुड़ियों का कालीन, दस दिनों तक हर सुबह रंगों का एक नया घेरा। बैकवाटर्स में लंबी-लंबी स्नेक बोट्स दौड़ लगाती हैं। केले के पत्ते पर सद्या परोसा जाता है, जिसमें तुम्हारी उंगलियों की गिनती से भी ज़्यादा पकवान होते हैं। किसी के आने का इंतज़ार है।","lang":"hi","body":"Every year at Onam, houses all over Kerala lay out a pookalam — a carpet of flower petals on the ground by the front door, a new ring of colour each morning for ten days. Long snake boats race down the backwaters. There is a sadya on a banana leaf with more dishes on it than you have fingers. Somebody is expected.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"उनका नाम महाबली है, और मलयाली बच्चे उन्हें मावेली कहते हैं। बहुत पहले वे यहाँ के राजा थे, और केरल आज तक उन्हें भूला नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"His name is Mahabali, and Malayali children call him Maveli. He was a king here, long ago, and Kerala has never got over him.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"कहते हैं कि उनके दौर में कोई झूठ नहीं बोलता था और कोई भूखा नहीं रहता था; दरवाज़ों पर ताले जैसी कोई चीज़ ही नहीं थी, क्योंकि किसी को भी कुछ छीनने या चुराने की ज़रूरत नहीं पड़ती थी। मावेली अपने देश में घूम-घूमकर लोगों से पूछते थे कि क्या उनके पास सब कुछ काफ़ी है। और उनके पास हमेशा सब कुछ काफ़ी होता था।","lang":"hi","body":"They say that in his time nobody lied and nobody went hungry; that there was no such thing as a lock on a door, because there was nothing anyone needed to take. Maveli walked about his country asking people whether they had enough. They always had.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"मावेली सबसे बढ़कर एक बात के लिए मशहूर थे: उन्होंने अपनी ज़िंदगी में कभी किसी माँगने वाले को ना नहीं कहा था। इसलिए जब एक छोटा-सा लड़का — लकड़ी की छतरी लिए, नंगे पाँव चलता हुआ एक नन्हा-सा ब्राह्मण बालक — उनके महायज्ञ में आया और उसने एक उपहार माँगा, तो पूरा दरबार मुस्कुरा उठा।","lang":"hi","body":"Maveli was famous for one thing above all: he had never in his life said no to anyone who asked him for something. So when a small boy — a very small brahmin boy, walking barefoot with a wooden umbrella — came to his great sacrifice and asked for a gift, the whole court smiled.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"\"कुछ भी माँग लो,\" मावेली ने कहा। \"तीन डग ज़मीन,\" बालक बोला। \"बस उतनी ही, जितनी मैं तीन क़दमों में नाप सकूँ।\" राजा के बूढ़े गुरु का चेहरा सफ़ेद पड़ गया और उन्होंने उनका हाथ पकड़ लिया। \"इसे कोई वचन मत दीजिए। मैं आपसे कह रहा हूँ। मत दीजिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Ask for anything,\" said Maveli. \"Three paces of land,\" said the boy. \"Just as much as I can cover in three steps.\" The king's old teacher went white and caught his arm. \"Do not promise this one anything. I am asking you. Do not.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"और वह छोटा-सा बालक बड़ा होने लगा। वह बढ़ता ही गया, यहाँ तक कि उसकी छतरी बादलों को छूने लगी। एक ही क़दम में समंदर से लेकर पहाड़ों तक पूरी धरती समा गई। दूसरे क़दम ने पूरे आकाश को नाप लिया। फिर वह एक पैर हवा में उठाए रुका और बोला: \"आपका वचन तो तीन का था। मैं तीसरा क़दम कहाँ रखूँ?\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the small boy began to grow. He grew until the umbrella brushed the clouds. One step covered the whole earth, from the sea to the mountains. The second step covered the sky. Then he stopped, with one foot in the air, and said: \"Your promise was three. Where shall I put the third?\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"मावेली ने उस पैर के नीचे अपने राज्य को देखा। फिर वे घुटनों के बल बैठ गए और अपना सिर झुका लिया। \"यहाँ,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"अब ऐसा कुछ नहीं बचा जो मेरा हो। वचन को टिकने के लिए भी तो कोई जगह चाहिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Maveli looked at his kingdom under that foot. Then he knelt down and bowed his head. \"Here,\" he said. \"There is nothing else left that is mine. A promise has to have somewhere to stand.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.mahabali-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.mahabali:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The King Who Comes Home Every Year","text":"तीसरा क़दम हौले से उनके सिर पर पड़ा, और मावेली केरल से विदा हो गए। लेकिन उनके माँगने पर उन्हें एक बात की छूट ज़रूर मिली: हर साल एक दिन लौटकर यह देखने की, कि उनकी प्रजा कुशल-मंगल से है या नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The third step came down softly, on the crown of his head, and Maveli went away from Kerala. But he had been given one thing back for the asking: one day every year to return and see whether his people are well.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-mahabali.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.mahabali|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"थार के रेगिस्तान के एक गाँव में, जब सारा काम निबट जाता है और रात ठंडी हो जाती है, तो भोपा नाम का एक गायक दो खंभों के बीच एक लंबा चित्रित कपड़ा फैलाता है। इसे फड़ कहते हैं। यह शुरू से आखिर तक छोटे-छोटे नारंगी और हरे चित्रों से भरा होता है, और चारों तरफ बिल्कुल अंधेरा रहता है जब तक कि उसकी पत्नी दीया उठाकर एक बार में उसका एक छोटा सा हिस्सा रोशन न कर दे।","lang":"hi","body":"In a village in the Thar desert, when the work is done and the night is cold, a singer called a bhopa unrolls a long painted cloth between two poles. It is called a phad. It is covered end to end with tiny orange and green figures, and it is completely dark until his wife holds up a lamp and lights one small patch of it at a time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"\"यहाँ,\" भोपा एक छड़ी से कपड़े को छूते हुए कहता है, \"अपनी काली घोड़ी केसर कालमी पर सवार, कोलू के पाबूजी हैं।\" और फिर वह गाने लगता है, और तब तक नहीं रुकता जब तक सूरज नहीं निकल आता।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Here,\" says the bhopa, touching the cloth with a stick, \"is Pabuji of Kolu, on his black mare, Kesar Kalmi.\" And then he sings, and does not stop until the sun comes up.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"पाबूजी रेगिस्तान के एक सरदार थे, और यही वह हिस्सा है जिसका सबको इंतज़ार रहता है। देवल नाम की एक औरत के पास मवेशियों का एक झुंड था, और एक सूखे के मौसम में वह पाबूजी के पास अपनी रक्षा की गुहार लेकर आई। उन्होंने उसे वचन दिया। उन्होंने कहा कि वह जब भी पुकारेगी, वह तुरंत आ जाएँगे — चाहे बुलावा आने के वक्त वह कुछ भी क्यों न कर रहे हों।","lang":"hi","body":"Pabuji was a chief of the desert, and this is the part everyone waits for. A woman called Deval kept a herd of cattle, and one dry season she came to him and asked for his protection. He gave her his word. Whenever she called, he said, he would come — whatever he was doing when the call came.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"महीनों बाद पाबूजी के अपने ब्याह का मौका था। उनकी कलाई पर रक्षा-सूत्र बँध चुका था, पवित्र अग्नि जल रही थी, और उन्होंने चार में से तीन फेरे पूरे कर लिए थे। वह अपनी दुल्हन के लिए एक ऐसा तोहफ़ा लाए थे जो उस रेगिस्तान में किसी दुल्हन को कभी नहीं मिला था: ऊँटनियों का एक झुंड, जो वहाँ किसी ने पहली बार देखा था।","lang":"hi","body":"Months later Pabuji was at his own wedding. The knot was tied at his wrist, the fire was lit, and he had walked three of the four rounds around it. He had brought his bride a gift no bride in that desert had ever been given: a herd of she-camels, the first anyone there had seen.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"चौथे फेरे के वक्त, देवल पैरों में धूल लपेटे दरवाज़े से भीतर आई। \"वे मेरे एक-एक मवेशी को हाँक कर ले गए हैं,\" उसने कहा। \"आपने मुझे सर्दियों में वचन दिया था। अब तो गर्मियाँ आ गई हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"On the fourth round, Deval came through the doorway with dust on her feet. \"They have driven off every one of my cattle,\" she said. \"You gave me your word in the winter. It is summer now.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"\"मुझे माफ़ करना,\" उन्होंने अपनी दुल्हन से कहा। \"सर्दियों में दिया गया वचन गर्मियों में भी वचन ही रहता है।\" उन्होंने केसर कालमी के लिए सीटी बजाई, और घोड़ी सरपट दौड़ती हुई आ पहुँची, और उस यात्रा की उड़ती धूल फड़ के ठीक बीचों-बीच चित्रित है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Forgive me,\" he said to his bride. \"A promise made in winter is still a promise in summer.\" He whistled for Kesar Kalmi, and the mare came at a run, and the dust of that ride is painted right across the middle of the phad.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.pabuji-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.pabuji:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Pabuji Leaves His Own Wedding","text":"वह मवेशियों को वापस ले आया। उसके बाद क्या हुआ, यह भोपा भोर से ठीक पहले के आखिरी पहर में गाता है, जब सबसे छोटे बच्चे अपनी माँओं की शॉल पर पहले ही सो चुके होते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"He brought the cattle back. What happened after that, the bhopa sings in the last hours before dawn, when the smallest children are already asleep on their mothers' shawls.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-pabuji.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.pabuji|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"एक बार लम्बिकिन नाम का एक नन्हा मेमना था, जो दुनिया से इतना खुश रहता था कि चलने के बजाय हर जगह फुदक-फुदक कर ही जाता था। एक सुबह वह गाते-बजाते जंगल के रास्ते अपनी नानी के घर निकला, क्योंकि नानी उसे हमेशा ज़रूरत से ज़्यादा ही खिलाती थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Once there was a Lambikin who was so pleased with the world that he skipped everywhere instead of walking. One morning he set off through the forest to his Granny's house, singing, because Granny always fed him far too much.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"पहले ही मोड़ पर एक सियार खड़ा था, जिसने अपने होंठ चाटे। \"लम्बिकिन! मैं तुम्हें खा जाऊँगा!\"","lang":"hi","body":"Round the first bend stood a Jackal, who licked his lips. \"Lambikin! I am going to EAT you!\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"\"अरे, मत खाओ,\" लम्बिकिन वहीं अपनी जगह पर फुदकते हुए बोला। \"मुझमें तो बस हड्डियाँ ही हड्डियाँ हैं। ज़रा नानी के यहाँ से मेरे लौटने का इंतज़ार करो — मैं मक्खन जैसा मोटा-ताज़ा हो जाऊँगा। तुम मुझे गुरुवार को खा लेना।\" सियार ने मक्खन के बारे में सोचा, और एक तरफ हट गया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Oh, don't,\" said Lambikin, skipping on the spot. \"I am all bones. Wait till I come back from Granny's — I shall be fat as butter. You can eat me on Thursday.\" The Jackal thought about butter, and stood aside.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"रास्ते में एक गिद्ध के साथ भी यही हुआ, फिर एक बूढ़े भालू के साथ, और आखिर में एक बाघ के साथ, जो उन सब में सबसे बड़ा और सबसे भूखा था। उन सब ने गुरुवार वाली बात सुनी। उन में से हर कोई एक तरफ हट गया।","lang":"hi","body":"It happened again with a vulture on the path, and again with an old bear, and finally with a Tiger, who was the largest and hungriest of the lot. Every one of them heard about Thursday. Every one of them stood aside.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"नानी के घर लैम्बिकिन ने हफ़्ते भर खूब छककर खाया, और हफ़्ते के अंत तक तो उससे ठीक से खड़ा भी नहीं हुआ जा रहा था। फिर उसने खिड़की से जंगल के रास्ते की तरफ देखा, जहाँ चार बड़े-बड़े साए चुपचाप एक कतार में बैठे गुरुवार का इंतज़ार कर रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"At Granny's house Lambikin ate for a week, and by the end of it he could hardly stand up. Then he looked out of the window at the forest path, where four large shapes were sitting patiently in a row, waiting for Thursday.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"रास्ते पर एक छोटा, गोल ढोल लुढ़कता हुआ और खुद ही गुनगुनाता हुआ आया: \"जंगल में खोया, तुम भी खोए! लिकटी, लिकटी, लिकटी टम!\"","lang":"hi","body":"Down the path came a small round drum, rolling and singing to itself: \"Lost in the forest, and so are you! On a lickety, lickety, lickety tum!\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lambikin-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lambikin:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lambikin and the Drumikin","text":"\"ड्रमकिन!\" सियार ने आवाज़ दी। \"क्या तुमने लैम्बिकिन को देखा है?\" \"जंगल में खोया, तुम भी खोए!\" ढोल ने गाया, और उसकी नाक के ठीक सामने से लुढ़क कर आगे निकल गया। गिद्ध ने पूछा। भालू ने पूछा। बाघ ने पूछा। ढोल ने उन सभी के सामने वही गाया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Drumikin!\" called the Jackal. \"Have you seen Lambikin?\" \"Lost in the forest, and so are you!\" sang the drum, and rolled straight past his nose. The vulture asked. The bear asked. The Tiger asked. The drum sang the same thing to all of them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lambikin.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lambikin|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"शुरू करने से पहले: इस कहानी में आप गुरु नानक के बारे में सुनेंगे, लेकिन उन्हें देखेंगे नहीं। सिख अपने गुरुओं के चित्र नहीं बनाते, इसलिए हम भी नहीं बनाएंगे। उनकी जगह आपको खंडा दिखेगा — और कहानी के बाकी सब लोग।","lang":"hi","body":"Before we start: in this story you will hear about Guru Nanak, but you will not see him. Sikhs do not make pictures of the Gurus, so we do not either. You will see the Khanda instead — and everyone else in the story.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"नानक पंजाब के एक गाँव के नौजवान थे, और उनके पिता मेहता कालू को उनकी चिंता रहती थी, जैसे आम तौर पर पिताओं को होती है। \"तुम बस ख्यालों में अपनी ज़िंदगी बिता रहे हो। ये बीस रुपये लो और पास के शहर जाओ। कुछ सस्ता खरीदो, उसे महंगे में बेचो और मुनाफा कमाकर घर लौटो। एक अच्छा सौदा — खरा सौदा। बाकी सब तो कर ही लेते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Nanak was a young man in a village in Punjab, and his father Mehta Kalu was worried about him, in the ordinary way that fathers worry. \"You are dreaming your life away. Take these twenty rupees to the next town. Buy something cheap, sell it dear, come home with a profit. A good bargain — a khara sauda. Everybody manages it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"उन्होंने नानक पर नज़र रखने के लिए घर के एक सेवक को साथ भेज दिया। सूरज निकलते ही दोनों एक कपड़े में बीस रुपये बांधकर निकल पड़े — उस ज़माने में यह बहुत बड़ी रकम थी, जिससे ढेर सारा नमक, कपड़ा या अनाज खरीदा जा सकता था।","lang":"hi","body":"He sent a family servant along to keep an eye on him. The two of them walked out at sunrise with twenty rupees knotted into a cloth — a serious amount of money then, enough to buy a great deal of salt or cloth or grain.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"आधे रास्ते में उन्हें सड़क किनारे पेड़ों के नीचे बैठे कुछ साधु मिले। वे बहुत दुबले-पतले थे। उन्होंने कई दिनों से कुछ नहीं खाया था, और वे कुछ मांग भी नहीं रहे थे, क्योंकि मांगना उनका तरीका नहीं था। नानक उनके साथ बैठ गए और पूछा कि कितने दिन हो गए हैं। उन्होंने कहा, तीन दिन। शायद चार।","lang":"hi","body":"Halfway there they came on a group of travelling holy men sitting under trees off the road. They were thin. They had eaten nothing for days, and they asked for nothing, because asking was not their way. Nanak sat down with them and asked how long it had been. Three days, they said. Perhaps four.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"सेवक ने उस बंधी हुई पोटली पर हाथ रखा। \"यह आपके पिताजी के पैसे हैं,\" उसने कहा। \"उन्होंने तो खरा सौदा करने को कहा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The servant put his hand on the knotted cloth. \"That is your father's money,\" he said. \"He asked for a bargain.\"","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"उन्होंने आटा, दाल और घी खरीदा, सड़क किनारे ही सब पकाया, और सबको तब तक खिलाया जब तक सबका पेट पूरी तरह भर नहीं गया। फिर नानक ने उस खाली कपड़े को झाड़ा और उसे हाथ में तह करके घर की ओर चल पड़े।","lang":"hi","body":"They bought flour and lentils and ghee, cooked it all at the roadside, and fed everybody until nobody wanted any more. Then Nanak wiped out the empty cloth and turned for home with it folded flat in his hand.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.sacha-sauda-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.sacha-sauda:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Truest Bargain","text":"गाँव की सीमा पर उनके पिता उनसे मिले। \"कहाँ है मेरा मुनाफ़ा?\" \"मैंने वही सौदा किया जो आपने कहा था,\" नानक ने कहा। \"सबसे सच्चा सौदा जो हो सकता है।\" मेहता कालू को यह जवाब ज़रा भी पसंद नहीं आया, और उन्होंने देर तक खूब खरी-खोटी सुनाई।","lang":"hi","body":"His father met him at the edge of the village. \"Where is my profit?\" \"I made the bargain you asked for,\" said Nanak. \"The truest one there is.\" Mehta Kalu did not think much of that answer at all, and said so at length.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-sacha-sauda.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.sacha-sauda|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"पंजाब में ब्यास नदी के किनारे गोइंदवाल में, गुरु अमर दास जी ने एक नियम बनाया था और वे किसी के लिए भी इसमें ढील नहीं देते थे: मुझसे मिलने से पहले, खाना खाइए। लंगर में। ज़मीन पर पंगत में बैठकर, जो भी वहाँ मौजूद हो उसके साथ, बाकी सब की तरह एक ही थाली में।","lang":"hi","body":"At Goindval, on the river Beas in Punjab, Guru Amar Das had made a rule and would not bend it for anybody: before you meet me, you eat. In the langar. Sitting on the floor in a row, with whoever else is there, off the same plate as everyone else.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"\"हर कोई?\" लोग पूछते। \"हर कोई,\" रसोई में दाल परोसते हुए सेवादार कहते। \"अमीर, गरीब, चाहे कोई पहली बार आया हो या सौवीं बार। बैठ जाइए, हाथ आगे बढ़ाइए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Everybody?\" people would ask. \"Everybody,\" said the sevadars in the kitchen, ladling out dal. \"Rich, poor, first time, hundredth time. Sit down, hold out your hands.\"","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"फिर एक दिन सड़क पर उड़ती धूल के बीच शहंशाह अकबर आते दिखे, अपने घोड़ों, शाही छतरियों और ढेरों ऐसे लोगों के साथ जिनका काम ही यह देखना था कि शहंशाह को कभी किसी चीज़ का इंतज़ार न करना पड़े।","lang":"hi","body":"Then one day the dust on the road turned out to be the Emperor Akbar, with horses, and umbrellas, and a great many people whose whole job was to make sure that nobody ever asked him to wait for anything.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"एक सेवादार हाथ पोंछते हुए बाहर आई। \"गुरु जी आपसे मिलेंगे,\" उसने कहा, \"जब आप भोजन कर लेंगे।\" वहाँ इतना गहरा सन्नाटा छा गया कि चम्मच भी खड़ी रह जाए। शहंशाह के एक आदमी ने कहा: \"जानती हो ये कौन हैं?\" \"हाँ,\" उसने कहा। \"उन्हें भूख लगी होगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A sevadar came out, wiping her hands. \"The Guru will see you,\" she said, \"after you have eaten.\" There was a silence you could have stood a spoon up in. One of the Emperor's men said: \"Do you know who this is?\" \"Yes,\" she said. \"He must be hungry.\"","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"अकबर ने लंगर के छोटे दरवाज़े की तरफ़ देखा, और अंदर ज़मीन पर पालथी मारकर कतारों में पहले से बैठे लोगों को देखा — किसान, मुसाफ़िर, बच्चे, और मिट्टी से सना एक कुम्हार।","lang":"hi","body":"Akbar looked at the low doorway of the langar hall, and the rows of people already sitting cross-legged on the floor inside — farmers, travellers, children, a potter still covered in clay.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"उन्होंने एक पत्तल पर मोटी रोटी और दाल खाई, एक तरफ़ किसान बैठा था और दूसरी तरफ़ एक बच्चा। खाना खत्म करने के बाद, वे थोड़ी देर और वहीं बैठे रहे। \"मैंने हिंदुस्तान की हर मेज़ पर खाना खाया है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"मुझे कभी किसी ने ज़मीन पर नहीं बिठाया। मुझे लगता है, मैं समझ गया हूँ कि आप ऐसा क्यों करते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He ate coarse roti and dal off a leaf plate, with a farmer on one side of him and a child on the other. When he had finished he sat there a moment longer than he needed to. \"I have eaten at every table in India,\" he said. \"Nobody has ever made me sit on the floor. I think I see why you do it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-sk.langar-akbar-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:sk.langar-akbar:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Emperor Sits on the Floor","text":"उन्होंने रसोई के लिए ज़मीन दान करने की पेशकश की। गुरु जी ने इसे लेने से मना कर दिया: लंगर आम लोगों से ही चलता है, नहीं तो वह लंगर ही नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"He offered a grant of revenue land for the kitchen. The Guru would not take it: a langar is fed by ordinary people or it is not a langar.","art":"art/story/sm/sk-langar-akbar.jpg","route":"#/story/sk.langar-akbar|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Guru's Way"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"1666 में, शिवाजी अपने नन्हे बेटे संभाजी के साथ बादशाह से मिलने उत्तर में आगरा गए। मुलाकात अच्छी नहीं रही। जब उन्होंने वहाँ से निकलना चाहा, तो पाया कि वे जा नहीं सकते: दरवाज़े पर सिपाही, रास्ते पर सिपाही—ऐसे सिपाही जो बेहद अदब से बात कर रहे थे, मगर अपनी जगह से टस से मस नहीं हो रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"In 1666 Shivaji rode north to Agra to meet the Emperor, with his young son Sambhaji beside him. The meeting went badly. When he tried to leave, he found that he could not: soldiers on the gate, soldiers on the road, soldiers who were extremely polite and would not move.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"\"आप बादशाह के मेहमान हैं,\" उन्होंने कहा—और यह एक ऐसा जुमला है जिसके दो बिल्कुल अलग मायने निकल सकते हैं, इस बात पर कि चौखट पर कौन खड़ा है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"You are the Emperor's guest,\" they said, which is a sentence that can mean two completely different things depending on who is standing in the doorway.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"शिवाजी अपने घर से हज़ारों मील दूर थे, एक अनजान शहर में, जहाँ दिन-रात उन पर पहरा रहता था। मुट्ठी भर आदमियों के साथ लड़कर बाहर निकलना कोई योजना नहीं थी। इससे तो बस सबकी जान ही जाती।","lang":"hi","body":"Shivaji was a thousand miles from home, in a city he did not know, watched day and night. Fighting his way out with a handful of men was not a plan. It was a way of getting everybody killed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"“मेरी तबीयत खराब है,” शिवाजी ने ऐलान किया, “और मैं ईश्वर का धन्यवाद कर रहा हूँ।” और फिर हर सुबह घर से साधु-संतों और आगरा के गरीबों के लिए मिठाइयों और फलों से भरे बड़े-बड़े चपटे टोकरे बाहर जाने लगे — इतने भारी कि दो-दो आदमी उन्हें डंडों के सहारे उठाते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"\"I am ill,\" Shivaji announced, \"and I am giving thanks.\" And out of the house each morning went great flat baskets of sweets and fruit for holy men and for the poor of Agra — carried on poles by two men each, because they were heavy.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"पहरेदार ढक्कन हटाते। वे पेड़ों के बीच अपने हाथ डालकर टटोलते। कुछ नहीं। अगले दिन भी वही। और उसके अगले दिन भी। हर सुबह ठीक उसी समय टोकरे बाहर जाते, और पहरेदारों की उँगलियाँ चिपचिपी हो जातीं, कमर दुखने लगती और वे पेड़े देख-देखकर बुरी तरह ऊब जाते।","lang":"hi","body":"The guards took the lids off. They dug about in the pedas with their hands. Nothing. The next day, the same. And the next. The baskets went out at the same hour every morning, and the guards got sticky fingers and sore backs and extremely tired of pedas.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"दूसरे हफ्ते तक वे तीन में से बस एक ही ढक्कन उठाकर देखते। तीसरे हफ्ते तक तो वे पूरे काफिले को हाथ हिलाकर जाने का इशारा कर देते और वापस अपनी छाँव में चले जाते। जो चीज़ बीस दिनों से उबाऊ लग रही हो, उस पर लगातार ध्यान टिकाए रखना वाकई बहुत मुश्किल होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"By the second week they were lifting one lid in three. By the third they were waving the whole procession through and going back to their shade. It is very hard to keep looking hard at something that has been boring for twenty days.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"एक शाम दो टोकरे रोज़ से ज़्यादा भारी होकर बाहर निकले। किसी ने ढक्कन नहीं उठाया। एक के अंदर शिवाजी दुबक कर बैठे थे। दूसरे के अंदर संभाजी थे, जो नौ साल के थे और जिन्हें सख्त हिदायत थी कि उन्हें छींकना बिल्कुल नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"One evening two of the baskets went out heavier than usual. Nobody lifted a lid. Inside one was Shivaji, folded up small. Inside the other was Sambhaji, who was nine years old and had been told he must not sneeze.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.shivaji-baskets-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.shivaji-baskets:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Baskets of Sweets","text":"उन्हें शहर से बाहर ले जाया गया, अंधेरे में नीचे उतारा गया, और वे गायब! वे ऐसे रास्तों से दक्कन अपने घर पहुँचे जिनका किसी ने अंदाज़ा भी नहीं लगाया था, और कहानी कहती है कि वे एक घूमंतू गायक के भेष में पहुँचे — जो कि बिल्कुल वैसा ही अंत है जिसकी यह कहानी हक़दार थी।","lang":"hi","body":"They were carried out of the city, set down in the dark, and gone. He rode home to the Deccan by roads nobody expected, and the story says he arrived dressed as a wandering singer, which is exactly the sort of ending this story deserves.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-shivaji-baskets.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.shivaji-baskets|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"\"ओडिशा के तट पर, पुरी में, राजा इंद्रद्युम्न उस किनारे पर सबसे बड़ा मंदिर बनाना चाहते थे। उनके पास दीवारें थीं। उनके पास शिखर थे। जो उनके पास नहीं था, वह यह था कि उनके भीतर क्या स्थापित किया जाए, और उनके सामने लाया गया कोई भी पत्थर सही नहीं बैठ रहा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At Puri, on the coast of Odisha, King Indradyumna wanted to build the greatest temple on that shore. He had the walls. He had the towers. What he did not have was what should stand inside them, and no stone he was offered was the right stone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"\"फिर एक सुबह मछुआरे दौड़ते हुए आए। लहरों के साथ बहकर लकड़ी का एक लट्ठा किनारे आ गया था — गहरे रंग की लकड़ी का एक विशाल कुंदा, जो पानी पर सीधा तैर रहा था, मानो कोई उसे चला रहा हो। बीस आदमी भी उसे उठा नहीं पाए। फिर एक बच्चे ने उसे धक्का दिया, और वह हिल गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then one morning the fishermen came running. A log had come in on the tide — a huge piece of dark wood, floating upright, riding the surf as though somebody were steering it. Twenty men could not lift it. Then a child pushed it, and it moved.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"\"ओडिशा का हर मूर्तिकार हाथ आजमाने आया। राज्य की सबसे बेहतरीन छेनियाँ मुड़ गईं, टूट गईं, या फिसल गईं। वह लकड़ी किसी से भी कटने का नाम नहीं ले रही थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every carver in Odisha came to try. The best chisels in the kingdom bent, snapped, or slid off. The wood would not be cut by anyone at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"\"महल के फाटक पर एक बूढ़ा बढ़ई दिखाई दिया — न किसी ने उसे पहले देखा था, और न किसी ने उसे आते देखा। \\\"मैं इसे बनाऊँगा,\\\" उसने कहा। \\\"एक शर्त है। मैं बंद दरवाज़े के पीछे काम करूँगा, और इक्कीस दिनों तक कोई उसे नहीं खोलेगा। न आप, महाराज। न कोई और।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"An old carpenter appeared at the palace gate — nobody had seen him before, and nobody saw him arrive. \"I will do it,\" he said. \"One condition. I work behind a shut door, and nobody opens it for twenty-one days. Not you, Maharaj. Not anybody.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"\"दरवाज़ा बंद कर दिया गया। अंदर से दिन-रात छेनी की आवाज़ आती रही, ठक, ठक, ठक — और पूरा शहर बाहर बैठा सुनता रहा और अंदाज़ा लगाता रहा। चौदहवें दिन आवाज़ आनी बंद हो गई।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The door was shut. From inside came chisel-sounds, day and night, thock, thock, thock — and the whole city sat outside listening to it and guessing. On the fourteenth day the sound stopped.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"रानी गुंडिचा पूरे दिन उस दरवाज़े के पास बैठी रहीं। कोई आवाज़ नहीं। पूरी रात। कोई आवाज़ नहीं। \"वे बंद कमरे में अकेले एक बूढ़े आदमी हैं,\" उन्होंने कहा, \"बिना पानी के। क्या पता वे अंदर फ़र्श पर पड़े हों?\"","lang":"hi","body":"The queen, Gundicha, sat by that door all day. No sound. All night. No sound. \"He is an old man alone in a shut room,\" she said, \"with no water. What if he is lying on the floor in there?\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"कमरा खाली था। न कोई बढ़ई, न लकड़ी का कोई बुरादा, और न ही ऐसा कोई दरवाज़ा जिससे वे बाहर निकल पाते। और फ़र्श के बीचों-बीच खड़ी थीं तीन मूरतें — बड़ी-बड़ी गोल आँखें, फैली हुई रंगी मुस्कानें, और आधे-अधूरे छूटे हाथ। बिल्कुल अधूरी।","lang":"hi","body":"The room was empty. No carpenter, no shavings, no door he could have gone out of. And standing there in the middle of the floor were three figures — huge round eyes, wide painted smiles, and arms that stopped short. Unfinished.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.unfinished-hands-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.unfinished-hands:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Carpenter Who Asked for a Closed Door","text":"राजा भागते हुए आए। सब इंतज़ार करने लगे कि वे कहेंगे: फिर से शुरू करो, किसी मूर्तिकार को बुलाओ, इन्हें ठीक से पूरा करो। वे बहुत देर तक वहीं खड़े रहे। फिर उन्होंने कहा: \"नहीं। ये हमारे पास जिस रूप में आए हैं, वैसे ही रहेंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The king came running. Everyone waited for him to say: start again, get a sculptor, finish them properly. He stood there a long time. Then he said: \"No. This is how they came to us. This is how they stay.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-unfinished-hands.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.unfinished-hands|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"नागा पहाड़ियों में बहुत ऊँचे, जहाँ गाँव चोटियों पर बसे हैं और बादल दरवाज़ों से सीधे भीतर चले आते हैं, हर बात की शुरुआत में यह किस्सा सुनाया जाता है। पहली माँ के तीन बेटे थे। एक आत्मा था। एक बाघ था। और एक इंसान था।","lang":"hi","body":"High in the Naga hills, where the villages sit on the tops of the ridges and the clouds come in through the doorways, they tell this at the start of everything. The first mother had three sons. One was the Spirit. One was the Tiger. One was the Man.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"वे सब एक ही घर में बड़े हुए, और कुछ समय तक सब ठीक-ठाक चलता रहा, जैसा कि आमतौर पर होता है। आत्मा रात भर जागता रहता। बाघ ढेर सारा खाना चट कर जाता और हड्डियाँ छोड़ देता। इंसान लकड़ी से तरह-तरह की चीज़ें बनाता और उनके बारे में अपनी बातें बंद ही नहीं करता था।","lang":"hi","body":"They grew up in one house, and it worked for a while, the way it does. The Spirit was up all night. The Tiger ate an enormous amount and left the bones. The Man made things out of wood and would not stop talking about them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"\"यह घर मेरा है,\" बाघ ने कहा, \"मैं सबसे ताक़तवर हूँ।\" \"यह मेरा है,\" आदमी ने कहा, \"दरवाज़ा मैंने बनाया है।\" आत्मा ने कुछ भी नहीं कहा, और किसी बहस में ऐसा करना सामने वाले को सबसे ज़्यादा चिढ़ाने वाली बात होती है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"This house is mine,\" said the Tiger, \"I am the strongest.\" \"It is mine,\" said the Man, \"I built the door.\" The Spirit said nothing at all, which is somehow the most annoying thing anybody can do in an argument.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"उनकी माँ बाहर बैठकर देर तक यह सब सुनती रहीं। वे बूढ़ी थीं और थकी हुई थीं, और वे जानती थीं कि वे तीनों ही अपनी जगह सही थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Their mother sat outside and listened to it for a long time, and she was old and she was tired, and she knew that all three of them were right.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"वे दौड़े। और यहीं से कहानियों के रास्ते अलग हो जाते हैं — कुछ गाँवों में आदमी ईमानदारी से जीतता है, तो कुछ में चालाकी से, और बड़े-बुज़ुर्ग आज भी आग के पास बैठकर इस बात पर बहस करते हैं। लेकिन इसके बाद क्या हुआ, इस बात को सब मानते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"They ran. And here the tellings pull apart — in some villages the Man wins fairly, in others he wins by being cunning about it, and elders will still argue about that around a fire. But everyone agrees on what happened afterwards.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"बाघ जंगल की तरफ़ चला गया। उसने कुछ ख़ास नहीं कहा। आत्मा पूरी तरह आँखों से ओझल हो गई, चट्टानों, पानी और ऊँचे पेड़ों के बीच, जहाँ आप उसे महसूस तो कर सकते हैं पर देख नहीं सकते। और आदमी के पास रह गया वह घर, वह आग और वह दरवाज़ा।","lang":"hi","body":"The Tiger went to the forest. He did not say much. The Spirit went out of sight altogether, into the rocks and the water and the tall trees where you can feel him but not see him. And the Man kept the house, and the fire, and the door.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.naga-brothers-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.naga-brothers:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Man, the Tiger and the Spirit","text":"\"कभी-कभार आकर खा लिया करना,\" पेड़ों के किनारे उनकी माँ ने बाघ से कहा। उसने एक बार मुड़कर उनकी तरफ़ देखा, और बस।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Come and eat sometimes,\" their mother said to the Tiger at the edge of the trees. He looked back at her once, and that was all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-naga-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.naga-brothers|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"मेघालय की खासी पहाड़ियों में — जो धरती की सबसे नम जगह है, जहाँ बादल गाँवों के बीच से होकर गुज़रते हैं — सूरज एक औरत हैं। लोग उन्हें 'का स्नगी' कहते हैं। चाँद उनका भाई है। और एक बार, बहुत समय पहले, कुछ ऐसा हुआ जिससे वे इतनी उदास हो गईं कि एक गुफ़ा में चली गईं और फिर बाहर ही नहीं निकलीं।","lang":"hi","body":"In the Khasi hills of Meghalaya — the wettest place on earth, where the clouds walk through the villages — the sun is a woman. Ka Sngi, they call her. The moon is her brother. And once, long ago, something happened that upset her so badly that she walked into a cave and would not come out.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"पूरी दुनिया में अंधेरा छा गया। रात जैसा अंधेरा नहीं, जो सुबह ढल जाता है। दूसरे वाला अंधेरा। धान का बढ़ना रुक गया। बच्चों का बाहर खेलना बंद हो गया। लोग भरी दोपहर में चीड़ की मशालें जलाने लगे और एक-दूसरे का चेहरा न देखने के आदी हो गए।","lang":"hi","body":"The world went dark. Not night-dark, which ends. The other kind. The rice stopped growing. The children stopped going outside. People burned pine torches in the middle of the afternoon and got used to not seeing each other's faces.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"जानवरों ने एक सभा बुलाई। \"मैं उन्हें वापस लाऊँगा,\" बाघ ने कहा, और गुफ़ा के मुहाने पर जाकर ज़ोर से दहाड़ा। पहाड़ हिल उठा। चमगादड़ छत से गिर पड़े। पर इसके सिवा कुछ भी नहीं हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"The animals held a meeting. \"I will fetch her,\" said the tiger, and went to the cave mouth and roared into it. The mountain shook. The bats fell off the roof. Nothing else happened at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"\"मुझे कोशिश करने दीजिए,\" हाथी ने कहा, और वह इतनी ज़ोर से चिंघाड़ा कि पेड़ पीछे झुक गए। फिर भालू ने कोशिश की। फिर हिरण ने, साँप ने, और बहुत सारे बेहद पक्के इरादे वाले पक्षियों ने। पर गुफ़ा में अंधेरा ही रहा और सूरज अंदर ही रहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Allow me,\" said the elephant, and trumpeted until the trees leaned back. Then the bear tried. Then the deer, and the snake, and a great many extremely determined birds. The cave stayed dark and the sun stayed in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"भीड़ के बिल्कुल पीछे एक मुर्गा खड़ा था। वह न तो बड़ा था। न ही डरावना था। वह ऐसा जीव था जिसकी तरफ कोई दोबारा मुड़कर भी न देखे।","lang":"hi","body":"At the back of the crowd stood a rooster. He was not large. He was not frightening. He was the sort of creature nobody looks at twice.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"\"सुप्रभात,\" मुर्गे ने अंधेरे की ओर कहा, जो ऐसे हालात में कहना थोड़ा अजीब था। \"मैंने आपको बहुत दिनों से नहीं देखा है। बाहर हर कोई आपका हाल-चाल पूछ रहा है। कोई भी नाराज़ नहीं है। बस सबको ठंड लग रही है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Good morning,\" said the rooster into the dark, which was a slightly odd thing to say in the circumstances. \"I have not seen you for a while. Everyone outside is asking after you. Nobody is angry. They are just cold.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.khasi-sun-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.khasi-sun:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sun Who Would Not Come Out","text":"काफ़ी देर तक सन्नाटा छाया रहा। फिर सूरज ने धीरे से कहा कि वह आएगी। लेकिन वह तभी आएगी जब वह उसे बुलाएगा — और उसे हर बार बुलाना पड़ेगा।","lang":"hi","body":"There was a long silence. Then the sun said, quietly, that she would come. But she would come only when he called for her — and she would want calling every single time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-khasi-sun.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.khasi-sun|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"सौराष्ट्र के एक गाँव में एक नन्हीं चिड़िया और एक कौआ रहते थे, नीम के एक ही पेड़ पर, ऐसी डालियों पर जो लगभग छू रही थीं। मई की एक तपती सुबह चिड़िया ने वही बात कही जो गुजरात में मई के महीने में सब कहते हैं: \"बारिश आने वाली है। हमें घर चाहिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In a village in Saurashtra there lived a little sparrow and a crow, in the same neem tree, on branches that nearly touched. One hot morning in May the sparrow said the thing everybody in Gujarat says in May: \"The rains are coming. We need houses.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"चिड़िया ने मोम जुटाना शुरू किया। जब वज़न ही एक चम्मच जितना हो, तो यह बड़ा धीमा काम होता है — मोमबत्ती बनाने वाले के फ़र्श से एक कतरा, मधुमक्खी के छत्ते से एक टुकड़ा, उन तपते हफ़्तों में एक बार में बस एक-एक कण, जबकि बाकी सब छाँव में बैठे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The sparrow gathered wax. That is slow work when you weigh as much as a spoon — a bead of it from a candle-maker's floor, a scrap from a beehive, one crumb at a time, all through the hot weeks, while everyone else sat in the shade.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"कौआ अपनी डाल से उसे देखता रहा। \"तुम धूल से घर बना रही हो,\" उसने कहा। \"मेरा वाला देखो।\" उसने एक ही दोपहर में गोबर और कीचड़ से जैसे-तैसे अपना घर खड़ा कर लिया था, वह आकार में तीन गुना बड़ा था, और वह अपने घर से बेहद खुश था।","lang":"hi","body":"The crow watched her from his branch. \"You are building a house out of DUST,\" he said. \"Look at mine.\" He had slapped his together out of dung and mud in an afternoon, and it was three times the size, and he was extremely pleased with it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"चिड़िया अपना काम करती रही। जून के आखिरी हफ़्ते तक उसका घर छोटा, चिकना और कसकर बंद हो चुका था, और कौआ उस पर इतनी बार हँस चुका था कि अब वह अपने वही मज़ाक दोहराने लगा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The sparrow kept going. By the last week of June her house was small and smooth and shut tight, and the crow had laughed at it so many times that he had begun repeating his jokes.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"फिर अरब सागर से मानसून वैसे ही उमड़कर आया जैसे आता है — कोई हल्की फुहार नहीं, बल्कि पानी की एक दीवार। मोम का घर वहीं टिका रहा और उस पर से बारिश का पानी बहता रहा। गोबर का घर पहले नरम पड़ा, फिर उदास सा हुआ, और फिर अंत में बस एक कीचड़ का पोखर बनकर रह गया जिसमें एक डंडी फंसी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Then the monsoon came in off the Arabian Sea the way it does — not a drizzle, a wall of water. The wax house sat there with the rain running off it. The dung house went soft, and then sad, and then it was a puddle with a stick in it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"आधी रात को दरवाज़े पर खटखटाहट हुई। बाहर पूरी तरह भीगा हुआ एक कौआ खड़ा था, जिसके पंख सिर से बिल्कुल चिपके हुए थे। \"चिड़िया,\" उसने कहा। \"प्लीज़।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At midnight there was a knock. A very wet crow stood outside with his feathers plastered flat to his head. \"Sparrow,\" he said. \"Please.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chakli-kagdo-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chakli-kagdo:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The House of Wax and the House of Dung","text":"\"अंदर आ जाओ,\" चिड़िया ने कहा। \"अपने पैर पोंछ लो। और अगले अप्रैल तुम हर सुबह मेरे साथ मोम इकट्ठा करोगे, जब तक कि हमारे दो घर न बन जाएँ।\" \"हर सुबह,\" कौए ने कहा, जो उसके फ़र्श पर पानी टपका रहा था और उस समय किसी भी बात पर राज़ी हो जाता।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Come in,\" said the sparrow. \"Wipe your feet. And next April you are gathering wax with me, every morning, until we have two houses.\" \"Every morning,\" said the crow, who was dripping on her floor and would have agreed to anything.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chakli-kagdo.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chakli-kagdo|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"यह कहानी बनने से पहले एक गीत है। कर्नाटक में बच्चे इसे ज़बानी याद करते हैं — 'धरणी मंडल मध्यदोलगे' — और जब यह गाया जाता है, तो बड़े-बड़े लोग भी खामोश हो जाते हैं। यह पुण्यकोटि नाम की एक गाय के बारे में है।","lang":"hi","body":"This one is a song before it is a story. Children in Karnataka learn it by heart — Dharani mandala madhyadolage — and grown men have been known to go quiet when it is sung. It is about a cow called Punyakoti.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"ग्वाले के साथ पूरा झुंड भोर होते ही चरने निकल जाता और सांझ ढले घर लौटता था। पुण्यकोटि सबसे अंत में घर लौटती थी, क्योंकि वही देखती थी कि कोई पीछे तो नहीं छूट गया। वह ऐसी ही थी। आगे के हिस्से के लिए यह बात याद रखना।","lang":"hi","body":"The herd went out to graze at dawn with the cowherd, and came home at dusk, and Punyakoti came home last because she was the one who checked that nobody had been left behind. That is who she was. Remember it for the next bit.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"एक शाम चट्टानों के पास वह गलत रास्ते पर मुड़ गई, और उनकी छाया से निकलकर एक बाघ रास्ते के बीच आकर खड़ा हो गया। उसने कहा, \"मैं तीन दिनों से भूखा हूँ, और तुम सीधे मेरे मुँह में चली आई हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One evening she took a wrong turn near the rocks, and a tiger came out of the shadow of them and stood across the path. \"I have been hungry for three days,\" he said, \"and you have walked straight into my mouth.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"\"मुझे पता है,\" पुण्यकोटी ने कहा। वह भागी नहीं। \"मैं आपसे बहस नहीं करूँगी। बस — मेरे बछड़े ने अभी दूध नहीं पिया है। मुझे उसके पास जाने दीजिए, उसे दूध पिलाने दीजिए, और सब बता देने दीजिए। फिर मैं वापस आकर ठीक यहीं खड़ी हो जाऊँगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"I know,\" said Punyakoti. She did not run. \"I will not argue with you. Only — my calf has not been fed. Let me go to him, and feed him, and tell him. Then I will come back and stand exactly here.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"यह सुनकर बाघ इतना हँसा कि उसे बैठना पड़ गया। उसने कहा, \"तो जाओ। जाकर अपने बछड़े को दूध पिलाओ।\" उसे पूरा यकीन था कि वह उसे दोबारा कभी नहीं देख पाएगा, और उसे इस तरह दरियादिली दिखाने में बड़ा मज़ा आ रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The tiger laughed at that until he had to sit down. \"Go on then,\" he said. \"Go and feed your calf.\" He was quite certain he would never see her again, and he was rather enjoying being generous about it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"उसने अपने बछड़े को दूध पिलाया। उसने झुंड को सब बताया। और पूरा झुंड बाड़े के फाटक पर आकर खड़ा हो गया ताकि वह बाहर न जा सके, बछड़ा उससे लिपट गया, और सब एक साथ बोलने लगे कि बाघ से किया गया वादा कोई असली वादा नहीं होता।","lang":"hi","body":"She fed her calf. She told the herd. And the whole herd stood in the gateway of the shed so she could not get out, and the calf held on to her, and everybody talked at once about how a promise made to a tiger is not a real promise.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"बाघ ने उसके आने की आवाज़ सुनी तो उसे अपने कानों पर यकीन नहीं हुआ। वह उसके सामने आकर रुक गई। उसने कहा, \"मैं आ गई हूँ। मैं तैयार हूँ।\" और बाघ बहुत, बहुत देर तक उसे देखता रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"The tiger heard her coming and did not believe his ears. She stopped in front of him. \"I have come,\" she said. \"I am ready.\" And the tiger looked at her for a long, long time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.punyakoti-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.punyakoti:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cow Who Came Back","text":"आखिरकार उसने कहा, \"मैंने अपनी पूरी ज़िंदगी इस जंगल में शिकार किया है, और यहाँ कभी किसी से हारा नहीं। आज रात मैं हार गया। घर जाओ।\" और वह रास्ते से हट गया और उसे अपने पास से गुज़र जाने दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"I have hunted this forest my whole life,\" he said at last, \"and I have never once been beaten in it. Tonight I have. Go home.\" And he moved out of the path and let her walk past him.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-punyakoti.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.punyakoti|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"भरत और बाहुबली भाई थे। उनके पिता राजा थे और उन्होंने राजपाट छोड़ दिया था, और अपने बेटों के बीच सब कुछ बाँट दिया था, और कुछ समय तक तो सब ठीक चला। फिर भरत ने फैसला किया कि धरती के हर राज्य को उनके आगे झुकना चाहिए — उनके छोटे भाई के राज्य को भी।","lang":"hi","body":"Bharata and Bahubali were brothers. Their father had been a king and had given up being a king, and had divided everything between his sons, and for a while that worked. Then Bharata decided that every kingdom in the land ought to bow to him — including his little brother's.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"\"बाकी सब झुक चुके हैं,\" दूतों ने बाहुबली से कहा। \"बाकी सब उनके भाई नहीं हैं,\" बाहुबली बोले। \"मैं नहीं झुकूँगा।\" और दोनों ने अपनी-अपनी सेनाएँ बुला लीं, और दोनों सेनाएँ मैदान के आमने-सामने एक-दूसरे को देखती खड़ी रहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Everyone else has bowed,\" the messengers told Bahubali. \"Everyone else is not his brother,\" said Bahubali. \"I will not.\" And both of them called up their armies, and the two armies stood looking at each other across a plain.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"फिर बूढ़े मंत्री दोनों के बीच में आगे आए। \"बात जो भी हो,\" उन्होंने कहा, \"यह आप दोनों के बीच की है। हज़ारों लोग, जो आप दोनों से कभी मिले तक नहीं, उन्हें इसके लिए क्यों चोट पहुँचे? इसे आप खुद ही सुलझा लें। तीन मुकाबले। जो जीता, वही जीता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then the old ministers walked out into the space between them. \"Whatever this is,\" they said, \"it is between the two of you. Why should thousands of people who have never met either of you be hurt over it? Settle it yourselves. Three contests. Whoever wins, wins.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"तो सेनाएँ बैठ गईं और देखने लगीं। पहले दोनों ने बिना पलक झपकाए एक-दूसरे को घूरा, और भरत ने पलक झपका दी। फिर वे पानी में लड़े, पानी की बड़ी-बड़ी बौछारें उड़ाते हुए, और भरत पानी में नीचे चले गए। फिर उन्होंने कुश्ती की, और बाहुबली ने अपने बड़े भाई को ज़मीन से पूरा ऊपर उठा लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"So the armies sat down and watched. First they stared at each other without blinking, and Bharata blinked. Then they fought in the water, throwing it in great sheets, and Bharata went under. Then they wrestled, and Bahubali lifted his elder brother clean off the ground.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"और बस बात खत्म — जीत हो गई, तीन में से तीन। बाहुबली ने उन्हें नीचे उतारा, और उनका मुक्का लगभग अपने-आप ही ऊपर उठ गया, क्योंकि लड़ाई के अंत में मुक्का यही तो करता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And that was it — over, won, three out of three. Bahubali set him down, and his fist came up almost by itself, because that is what a fist does at the end of a fight.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"\"मैं यह क्या कर रहा हूँ?\" बाहुबली दोनों सेनाओं के सामने ज़ोर से बोले। \"मैंने अपने ही भाई से पूरी दुनिया जीत ली। और मुझे मिला क्या? दुनिया। यह तो हमेशा दुनिया ही रहने वाली थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"What am I doing?\" said Bahubali, out loud, in front of two armies. \"I have won the whole world off my own brother. And what have I got? The world. It was always going to be the world.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.bahubali-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.bahubali:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fist That Stopped","text":"उन्होंने भरत को राज्य सौंप दिया। फिर वे मैदान छोड़कर जंगल में चले गए, और वहाँ बिल्कुल शांत खड़े हो गए, और बहुत लंबे समय तक वैसे ही खड़े रहे — कहते हैं कि पूरे एक साल तक बिना हिले-डुले, यहाँ तक कि उनके पैरों के पास बांबियाँ बन गईं, पैरों पर लताएँ चढ़ गईं और उनके बालों में पक्षियों ने घोंसले बना लिए।","lang":"hi","body":"He gave the kingdom to Bharata. Then he walked off the field and into the forest, and stood still there, and went on standing still for a very long time — a year, they say, without moving, until anthills rose at his feet and creepers grew up his legs and birds nested in his hair.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-bahubali.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.bahubali|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"दूर देश से एक विद्वान राजा कृष्णदेवराय के दरबार में आया। उसके पास एक मखमली कपड़ा था, एक छोटा डिब्बा था, और अंदाज़ ऐसा था जैसे वह पहले ही मान चुका हो कि इस पूरे कमरे में सबसे अक्लमंद वही है।","lang":"hi","body":"A scholar came to the court of Krishnadevaraya from a long way off, with a velvet cloth and a small box, and the manner of a man who has already decided he is the cleverest person in the room.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"उसने तीन गुड़ियों से कपड़ा हटाया। एक जैसा नाप, एक जैसी लकड़ी, एक जैसा रंग, एक जैसा चेहरा। \"इनमें से एक,\" उसने कहा, \"लाख रुपये की है। एक हज़ार की है। और एक कौड़ी की भी नहीं है। मुझे बताइए कौन-सी कौन-सी है। आपका दरबार बहुत मशहूर है। चलिए, देखते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He unwrapped three dolls. Same size, same wood, same paint, same face. \"One of these,\" he said, \"is worth a lakh. One is worth a thousand. One is worth nothing whatever. Tell me which is which. Your court is famous. Let us see.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"मंत्रियों ने उन्हें तौला: बिल्कुल बराबर। ठोक-बजाकर देखा: बिल्कुल एक जैसी। दीये की रोशनी में ऊपर उठाया, उलट-पुलट कर देखा और दो दिन तक बहस करते रहे। विद्वान हाथ बाँधे बैठे रहे और खूब मज़ा लेते रहे।","lang":"hi","body":"The ministers weighed them: identical. Tapped them: identical. Held them up to the lamp, turned them over, argued for two days. The scholar sat with his hands folded and enjoyed himself enormously.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"तीसरे दिन तेनाली रामकृष्ण देर से टहलते हुए आए, गुड़ियों को बस उतनी ही देर देखा जितनी देर छींक आने में लगती है, और एक पतला सा धागा माँगा।","lang":"hi","body":"On the third day Tenali Ramakrishna wandered in late, looked at the dolls for about as long as it takes to sneeze, and asked for a piece of thin thread.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"उन्होंने पहली गुड़िया के कान में धागा डाला। वह सीधे दूसरे कान से बाहर निकल आया और वहीं लटक गया। \"यह वाली,\" तेनाली बोले, \"आपकी कही हर बात सुनती है और वह सीधे आर-पार निकल जाती है। अंदर कुछ नहीं ठहरता। इसकी कोई कीमत नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He fed the thread into the first doll's ear. It came straight out of the other ear and hung there. \"This one,\" said Tenali, \"hears everything you say and it goes clean through. Nothing stays. Worth nothing.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"उन्होंने दूसरी में धागा डाला। वह मुँह से बाहर निकल आया। \"यह आपकी बात सुनती है और तुरंत पूरे मोहल्ले को बता देती है। कीमत एक हज़ार — आप इसका इस्तेमाल कर सकते हैं, पर किसी ऐसी बात के लिए कभी नहीं जो आपके लिए मायने रखती हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He threaded the second. It came out of the mouth. \"This one hears what you tell it and immediately tells the whole street. Worth a thousand — you can use it, but never for anything you mind about.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.tenali-dolls-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.tenali-dolls:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Dolls and a Piece of Thread","text":"उन्होंने तीसरी में धागा डाला। धागा अंदर गया, रुका और वहीं टिक गया। उन्होंने धीरे से खींचा। वह कहीं से बाहर नहीं निकला। \"और यह वाली,\" तेनाली बोले, \"जो आप इसे देते हैं, उसे संभालकर रखती है। कीमत एक लाख, और इस दाम पर भी बहुत सस्ती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He threaded the third. The thread went in, and stopped, and stayed. He pulled gently. It did not come out anywhere. \"And this one,\" said Tenali, \"keeps what you give it. A lakh, and cheap at the price.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-tenali-dolls.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.tenali-dolls|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"उत्तर बिहार के मिथिला में लोग गोनू झा के किस्से वैसे ही सुनाते हैं जैसे दूसरी जगहों पर बीरबल के — राजा के दरबार का एक ऐसा आदमी, जो देखने में जितना सीधा-सादा लगता था, असल में उतना था नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"In Mithila, in north Bihar, they tell stories about Gonu Jha the way other places tell them about Birbal — a man at the Raja's court who was never quite as harmless as he looked.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"एक शाम राजा ने बैंगन की सब्ज़ी खाई और खुशी से चहक उठे। “सब्ज़ियों का राजा!” उन्होंने कहा। “राजाओं जैसा ही बैंगनी! मीठा! मुलायम! हम इसके सिवा कुछ और खाते ही क्यों हैं?”","lang":"hi","body":"One evening the Raja ate a dish of brinjal and went off like a firework. \"The KING of vegetables!\" he said. \"Purple as a king should be! Sweet! Soft! Why do we eat anything else?\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"“महाराज, यह बात तो आपने किसी भी कवि से बेहतर कही है,” गोनू झा तुरंत बोले। “बैंगन के सिर पर तो ताज होता है। सब्ज़ी तक को पता है कि वह शाही है।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Maharaj, you have said it better than any poet,\" said Gonu Jha at once. \"The brinjal wears a crown on its head. Even the vegetable knows it is royal.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"अगले मंगलवार राजा ने कुछ ज़्यादा ही बैंगन खा लिया और पूरी रात पेट के हाल पर पछताते रहे। “इसे यहाँ से हटाओ,” वे कराहते हुए बोले। “कड़वी, तेलिया, बेकार चीज़। इसे दोबारा रसोई में कभी मत आने देना।”","lang":"hi","body":"The following Tuesday the Raja had eaten rather too much brinjal and had spent the night regretting it in some detail. \"Take it away,\" he groaned. \"Bitter, oily, useless thing. Never let it in the kitchen again.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"“बिल्कुल सही बात, महाराज,” गोनू झा बोले। “निहायत ही रद्दी सब्ज़ी है। सिर पर जो ताज है, वह भी तो बस काँटे ही हैं।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Quite right, Maharaj,\" said Gonu Jha. \"A miserable vegetable. Even the crown on its head is only thorns.\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"पूरा दरबार चौकन्ना होकर बैठ गया। एक मंत्री ने सीधे उनकी ओर उँगली उठाई। “पिछले हफ़्ते आपने इसे शाही कहा था! इस हफ़्ते आप इसे काँटे बता रहे हैं! दोनों बातें एक साथ कैसे हो सकती हैं!”","lang":"hi","body":"The whole court sat up. A minister pointed straight at him. \"Last week you called it royal! This week you call it thorns! You cannot have both!\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.gonu-brinjal-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.gonu-brinjal:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Gonu Jha and the Brinjal","text":"\"महाराज,\" गोनू झा ने कहा, \"मैं आपका सेवक हूँ। मैं बैंगन का सेवक नहीं हूँ। वह मुझे कुछ नहीं देता।\" पूरा दरबार ठहाकों से गूँज उठा। राजा इतना हँसे कि आँखों में आँसू आ गए — और फिर अचानक रुक गए, क्योंकि बात कुछ उल्टी पड़ गई थी।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Maharaj,\" said Gonu Jha, \"I am your servant. I am not the brinjal's servant. It does not pay me anything.\" The court roared. The Raja laughed until his eyes watered — and then stopped, because something had gone in sideways.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-gonu-brinjal.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.gonu-brinjal|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"एक खेत में सौ बटेरें रहती थीं। एक बहेलिया रोज़ भोर में आता, बटेर की तरह तब तक सीटी बजाता जब तक कि वे उसके पास न आ जाएँ, और उन सब पर अपना जाल फेंक देता। इससे उसका तो बड़ा फ़ायदा होता था। बटेरों का नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"A hundred quails lived in a field, and a fowler used to come at dawn, whistle like a quail until they came to him, and throw his net over the lot of them. He did very well out of it. The quails did not.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"उनके सरदार ने लंबी घास में एक सभा बुलाई। \"वह अकेला आदमी है,\" उसने कहा। \"हम सौ पंछी हैं। उस जाल में सौ छेद हैं और तुम सबके पास एक-एक सिर है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Their leader called a meeting in the long grass. \"He is one man,\" he said. \"We are a hundred birds. There are a hundred holes in that net and each of you has a head.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"अगली सुबह जाल नीचे गिरा — और सीधे वापस ऊपर उठ गया। सौ बटेरें उसे बाड़ के ऊपर से, तालाब के ऊपर से उड़ा ले गईं, और सलीके से एक काँटेदार झाड़ी पर गिरा दिया, और नीचे से फिसलकर नाश्ते के लिए अपने घर चली गईं।","lang":"hi","body":"The next morning the net came down — and went straight back up again. A hundred quails carried it over the hedge, over the pond, and dropped it neatly onto a thorn bush, and slipped out from underneath and went home to breakfast.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"अगले दिन भी ऐसा ही हुआ। और उसके अगले दिन भी। बहेलिए की सुबहें काँटेदार झाड़ियों तक जाने और अपना जाल सुलझाने में बीतने लगीं, और इस बारे में उसकी पत्नी की भी अपनी राय थी, जो उसने उसे अच्छी-खासी तफ़सील से सुनाई।","lang":"hi","body":"It happened again the next day. And the next. The fowler spent his mornings walking to thorn bushes and untangling his own net, and his wife had opinions about it that she shared at some length.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"फिर एक सुबह, खेत में उतरते समय, एक बटेर का पंख दूसरी के सिर से टकरा गया। \"तुमने यह जानबूझकर किया।\" \"मैंने नहीं किया।\" \"तुम हमेशा बहुत ज़ोर से पंख फड़फड़ाते हो।\" \"तुम हमेशा बहुत देर से फड़फड़ाते हो।\" और पूरा खेत ज़ोर-शोर से किसी न किसी की तरफ़ हो गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Then one morning, landing in the field, one quail's wing clipped another's head. \"You did that on purpose.\" \"I did not.\" \"You always flap too hard.\" \"You always flap too LATE.\" And the whole field took a side, loudly.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"बहेलिया भोर में आया और उसने सीटी बजाई, और जाल नीचे गिरा। \"उठाओ!\" सरदार चिल्लाया। और आधा खेत चिल्लाया \"तुम उठाओ!\" और बाकी आधा चिल्लाया \"नहीं, तुम उठाओ!\" — और जाल एक इंच भी नहीं हिला।","lang":"hi","body":"The fowler came at dawn and whistled, and the net came down. \"LIFT!\" shouted the leader. And half the field shouted \"You lift!\" and the other half shouted \"No, YOU lift!\" — and the net did not move so much as an inch.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.quails-net-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.quails-net:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Quails Who Flew Off With the Net","text":"मुखिया ने यह खतरा तीन दिन पहले ही भाँप लिया था, और जो पक्षी अब भी उनकी बात सुनते थे, उन्हें वे पहले ही किसी दूसरे खेत में ले गए थे। बाद में वे हमेशा यही कहते थे कि उन्हें जाल ने नहीं हराया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The leader had seen it coming three days earlier, and had already taken the birds who would still listen to him to a different field. He always said afterwards that it was not the net that beat them.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-quails-net.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.quails-net|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"पेड़ों के किनारे गाँव वालों ने उन्हें जा पकड़ा, सब एक साथ बोलने लगे, \"उस रास्ते से नहीं। उस रास्ते पर एक विषैला साँप रहता है — चंडकौशिक। उसके पेड़ के चारों तरफ़ की घास देखिए, वह जली हुई है। घूमकर चले जाइए। बस एक दिन ज़्यादा लगेगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The villagers caught up with him at the edge of the trees, all talking at once. \"Not that way. There is a serpent on that path — Chandkaushik. Look at the grass round his tree, it is burnt. Go round. It is only one day longer.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"\"धन्यवाद,\" महावीर ने कहा। \"जो ग़ुस्से में हो, उसके लिए एक दिन भी बहुत लंबा समय होता है।\" और वे अंदर चले गए।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Thank you,\" said Mahavira. \"One day is a long time to somebody who is angry.\" And he walked in.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"रास्ता सुनसान और बहुत शांत था। न कोई पक्षी। न कोई कीड़ा-मकोड़ा। वे तब तक चलते रहे जब तक उस पेड़ तक नहीं पहुँच गए जिसके बारे में गाँव वालों ने बताया था, और फिर वे रुक गए, सीधे खड़े हो गए, अपनी आँखें मूँद लीं, और बिल्कुल भी नहीं हिले।","lang":"hi","body":"The path was empty and very quiet. No birds. No insects. He walked until he came to the tree the villagers had described, and then he stopped, and stood, and closed his eyes, and did not move at all.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"चंडकौशिक तेज़ी से बाहर निकला। उसने अपनी पूरी ज़िंदगी लोगों की चीखें सुनते, डंडों की मार खाते और लोगों को खुद से भागते देखकर बिताई थी — और हर बार इससे उसका ग़ुस्सा और बढ़ता गया, यहाँ तक कि उसके भीतर ग़ुस्से के सिवा लगभग कुछ बचा ही नहीं था। उसने उस पुरुष के पैर पर डंक मारा।","lang":"hi","body":"Chandkaushik came out fast. He had spent his whole life being screamed at, hit with sticks, run from — and every single time it had made him angrier, until anger was more or less all there was left of him. He struck at the man's foot.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"सांप ने फिर डसा। और फिर वह रुक गया, क्योंकि कुछ गड़बड़ थी। वह आदमी गिरा नहीं था। वह आदमी चीखा नहीं था। और उसके पैर के निशान से जो बह रहा था, वह लाल नहीं था। वह दूध जैसा सफ़ेद था।","lang":"hi","body":"The snake struck again. And then he stopped, because something was wrong. The man had not fallen. The man had not shouted. And what was running from the mark on his foot was not red. It was white as milk.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"महावीर ने अपनी आँखें खोलीं और नीचे उसकी तरफ़ देखा, और बड़ी शांति से बस इतना कहा: \"समझो, चंडकौशिक। समझो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Mahavira opened his eyes and looked down at him, and said only this, quite quietly: \"Understand, Chandkaushik. Understand.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jn.chandkaushik-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jn.chandkaushik:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Snake Everybody Ran From","text":"कहानी कहती है कि सांप बड़ी देर तक एकदम शांत पड़ा रहा, फिर वापस अपने पेड़ के नीचे चला गया, और उसने फिर कभी किसी पर हमला नहीं किया। गाँव वाले देखने बाहर निकले, पहले डरते-डरते, फिर बिना किसी डर के, और कुछ ही समय बाद बच्चे स्कूल जाने के लिए उसी छोटे रास्ते का इस्तेमाल करने लगे।","lang":"hi","body":"The story says the snake lay very still for a long time, and then went back under his tree, and never struck at anything again. The villagers came out to look, cautiously, then less cautiously, and after a while children were using the short path to school.","art":"art/story/sm/jn-chandkaushik.jpg","route":"#/story/jn.chandkaushik|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Jain Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"कश्मीर के एक राजा को साधारण कपड़ों में अपने राज्य में घूमना पसंद था, क्योंकि साधारण कपड़ों में राजा को वे बातें पता चल जाती हैं जो मुकुट पहने राजा को कभी नहीं पता चलतीं। एक लंबी दोपहर, वे नगर की ओर जा रही उसी सड़क पर एक किसान के साथ-साथ चलने लगे।","lang":"hi","body":"A king of Kashmir liked to walk about his country in ordinary clothes, because a king in ordinary clothes finds out things a king in a crown never will. One long afternoon he fell into step with a farmer going the same way along the road to the town.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"वे लगभग एक मील चुपचाप चल चुके थे, तभी किसान ने कहा: \"मैं आपको उठाऊँ, या आप मुझे उठाएँगे?\"","lang":"hi","body":"They had walked about a mile in silence when the farmer said: \"Shall I carry you, or will you carry me?\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"राजा ने उसे देखा। किसान एक छोटा-सा आदमी था जिसके पास एक गठरी थी। राजा एक भारी-भरकम आदमी थे और उनके हाथ में कुछ नहीं था। \"मुझे उठाओगे?\" उन्होंने कहा। \"हम दोनों भले-चंगे हैं। हम दोनों चल रहे हैं। यह कैसा सवाल है?\" किसान कुछ नहीं बोला और आगे चलता रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"The king looked at him. The farmer was a small man carrying a bundle. The king was a large man carrying nothing. \"Carry me?\" he said. \"We are both perfectly well. We are both walking. What sort of a question is that?\" The farmer said nothing and walked on.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"आगे चलकर वे पके हुए गेहूँ के एक खेत के पास से गुज़रे, जो ऊँचा और सुनहरा खड़ा था और उसमें कोई नहीं था। \"क्या वह खेत खाया जा चुका है,\" किसान ने पूछा, \"या नहीं?\" \"खाया हुआ?\" राजा ने कहा। \"वह तो तुम्हारे ठीक सामने खड़ा है। उसे किसी ने छुआ तक नहीं है।\" किसान कुछ नहीं बोला और आगे चलता रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"Further along they passed a field of ripe wheat, standing tall and gold with nobody in it. \"Is that field eaten,\" asked the farmer, \"or not?\" \"Eaten?\" said the king. \"It is standing right there in front of you. Nothing has touched it.\" The farmer said nothing and walked on.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"शहर के छोर पर वे एक शवयात्रा के पास से गुज़रे। \"वह आदमी ज़िंदा है,\" किसान ने पूछा, \"या मर चुका है?\" राजा तंग आ चुके थे। \"साफ़ दिख तो रहा है कि वह मर चुका है।\" चौराहे पर किसान रुका और बड़े प्यार से बोला, \"आप ज्ञानी तो हैं, पर आपको कुछ भी नहीं पता,\" और अपने घर की ओर मुड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"At the edge of the town they passed a funeral. \"Is that man alive,\" asked the farmer, \"or dead?\" The king had had enough. \"You can see he is dead.\" At the crossroads the farmer stopped and said, quite kindly, \"You are a learned man. But you do not know anything,\" and turned for home.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"घर पहुँचकर किसान ने अपनी बेटी को रास्ते में मिले उस अजीब, अच्छे कपड़े पहने आदमी के बारे में बताया, तो उसने अपना काम एक तरफ़ रख दिया और हँस पड़ी। \"अब्बा! उन्हें तो कुछ भी समझ नहीं आया, है ना?\"","lang":"hi","body":"At home the farmer told his daughter about the odd, well-dressed man on the road, and she put down what she was doing and laughed. \"Abba. He did not understand any of it, did he?\"","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-wt.kashmir-carry-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:wt.kashmir-carry:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Shall I Carry You, or Will You Carry Me?","text":"वह बोली, \"\"मुझे उठाकर चलो\" का मतलब है कि कोई कहानी सुनाओ ताकि रास्ता छोटा लगे। \"क्या खेत खाया जा चुका है?\" का मतलब है: क्या किसान ने उस फ़सल के बदले पहले ही कर्ज़ ले लिया है — क्योंकि अगर ले लिया है, तो फ़सल खेत में खड़ी हो या न हो, वह तो खाई जा चुकी। \"क्या आदमी ज़िंदा है?\" का मतलब है: क्या वह अपने पीछे ऐसे बच्चे छोड़ गया है जो उसे याद रखेंगे — क्योंकि अगर छोड़ गया है, तो वह पूरी तरह से गया नहीं है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Carry me\" means tell me a story to shorten the road, she said. \"Is the field eaten?\" means: has the farmer already borrowed money against that crop — because if he has, then it is eaten, standing there or not. \"Is the man alive?\" means: has he left children who will remember him — because if he has, then he is not entirely gone.","art":"art/story/sm/wt-kashmir-carry.jpg","route":"#/story/wt.kashmir-carry|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Clever Ones"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lingo-song-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lingo-song:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lingo and the First Song","text":"मध्य भारत के गोंड लोग — यानी छत्तीसगढ़ और मध्य प्रदेश के जंगलों और पहाड़ियों के लोग — लिंगो की कहानी सुनाते हैं, जो सबसे पहले आए और उन्होंने बाकी सबके लिए रास्ते निकाले। गाने वाले कहते हैं कि गोंडों के पास आज जो ज़्यादातर चीज़ें हैं, लिंगो ही जाकर उन्हें लाए थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The Gond people of central India — the forests and hills of Chhattisgarh and Madhya Pradesh — tell of Lingo, who came first and worked things out for everybody else. Most of what the Gonds have, the singers say, Lingo went and fetched.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lingo-song.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lingo-song|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lingo-song-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lingo-song:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lingo and the First Song","text":"एक शाम लिंगो बैठकर जंगल को सुनने लगे, और उन्हें उसमें होने वाली हर चीज़ सुनाई दे रही थी। पत्थरों के ऊपर से बहता पानी। आपस में टकराते बाँस। मधुमक्खियाँ। घाटी के दूर वाले छोर से शुरू होकर उनकी तरफ़ आती बारिश। \"यह सब तो बस आवाज़ें हैं,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"इनमें से कोई भी गीत नहीं है। गीत तो ऐसा होना चाहिए जो लौटकर वापस आ सके।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One evening Lingo sat and listened to the forest, and he could hear everything in it. Water over stones. Bamboo knocking. Bees. Rain starting at the far end of the valley and coming towards him. \"All of that is sound,\" he said. \"None of it is a song. A song has to be able to come back.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lingo-song.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lingo-song|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lingo-song-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lingo-song:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lingo and the First Song","text":"उन्होंने सीटी बजाने की कोशिश की, पर वह हवा में उड़ गई। उन्होंने दो लकड़ियों को आपस में बजाकर देखा, आवाज़ तो अच्छी थी पर वह गीत नहीं था। उन्होंने चिड़ियों से वही दोबारा गाने को कहा, और चिड़ियों ने बड़ी समझदारी से समझाया कि वे कभी भी कोई चीज़ दो बार एक ही तरह से नहीं करतीं।","lang":"hi","body":"He tried whistling and it blew away. He tried banging two sticks, which is a good noise but not a song. He tried getting the birds to do it again, and the birds pointed out, reasonably, that they never do anything the same way twice.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lingo-song.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lingo-song|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lingo-song-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lingo-song:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lingo and the First Song","text":"इसलिए उनके पास जो कुछ था, वे वही लेकर बैठ गए: एक सूखी खाली लौकी, लकड़ी का एक टुकड़ा, और डोरी की तरह बटे हुए कुछ रेशे।","lang":"hi","body":"So he sat with what he had: a dry gourd with nothing in it, a length of wood, and some fibre twisted into cord.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lingo-song.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lingo-song|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lingo-song-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lingo-song:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lingo and the First Song","text":"वह सुर घाटी के पार गया और दूर पहाड़ी से टकराकर वापस लौट आया। लिंगो ने तार को दूसरी बार छेड़ा यह देखने के लिए कि क्या वह दोबारा ऐसा करेगा। उसने वैसा ही किया। वे आधी रात तक वहीं बैठे यह पता लगाते रहे कि वह और क्या-क्या कर सकता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The note went out across the valley and came home again off the far hill. Lingo pulled the string a second time to see whether it would do it twice. It did. He sat there half the night finding out what else it would do.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lingo-song.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lingo-song|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Tales from Every Corner"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]}});
